Mmm. Yeah, nice try, Eddie.

251
00:21:56,417 --> 00:21:59,333
I hope you rap better than you prank
or I'm out two bucks.

252
00:21:59,417 --> 00:22:02,167
<i>Eddie's in lane one,
driving his first Maybach.</i>

253
00:22:03,917 --> 00:22:07,292
Come on, lanes.
See how many bins I got over here…

254
00:22:09,083 --> 00:22:12,500
Pay stubs, bills, family photos.
Anything we can use.

255
00:22:19,708 --> 00:22:21,125
<i>Just relax, okay?</i>

256
00:22:22,542 --> 00:22:25,542
<i>This is how it goes, Ethan.
Soon an associate of mine</i>

257
00:22:25,625 --> 00:22:27,583
<i>is gonna step into your line
with a boarding pass</i>

258
00:22:27,667 --> 00:22:30,875
<i>for Northwind Flight 1850
non-stop to JFK.</i>

259
00:22:30,958 --> 00:22:35,042
<i>You are gonna make sure
that his bag clears the machine.</i>

260
00:22:35,125 --> 00:22:36,542
This is a joke, right?

261
00:22:36,625 --> 00:22:39,375
<i>Is anything I just said funny?</i>

262
00:22:39,458 --> 00:22:40,458
No.

263
00:22:41,167 --> 00:22:44,000
<i>If it's any consolation,
you were not my first choice.</i>

264
00:22:44,083 --> 00:22:46,417
<i>You're not where
you're supposed to be today,</i>

265
00:22:46,500 --> 00:22:49,667
<i>but that is okay. To be honest,
it makes my day a little easier.</i>

266
00:22:50,208 --> 00:22:52,750
Okay. I'll play along.

267
00:22:52,833 --> 00:22:55,500
- What's in the bag?
<i>- Diamonds out of Papua New Guinea.</i>

268
00:22:55,583 --> 00:22:57,083
- Bullshit.
<i>- Okay.</i>

269
00:22:57,167 --> 00:22:58,458
You answered too quickly.

270
00:22:58,542 --> 00:23:01,000
<i>Yeah, maybe because knowing
won't change anything</i>

271
00:23:01,083 --> 00:23:04,583
<i>and I hope I don't have to execute
someone close to you to prove it.</i>

272
00:23:05,958 --> 00:23:09,083
<i>Jason's house is right nearby,
a nice rental on Sixth Street.</i>

273
00:23:10,417 --> 00:23:12,792
<i>Rochelle is home with the twins.</i>

274
00:23:14,042 --> 00:23:16,167
<i>Why don't you ask me
if I know their names?</i>

275
00:23:17,333 --> 00:23:18,375
Who are you?

276
00:23:18,458 --> 00:23:21,958
<i>I'm just a traveler headed home
for the holidays, like everyone else.</i>

277
00:23:22,042 --> 00:23:23,542
<i>Probably a lot like you.</i>

278
00:23:23,625 --> 00:23:25,958
<i>If we met on the softball field,
I bet we'd be buddies.</i>

279
00:23:26,042 --> 00:23:28,958
<i>We'd go out for beers after.
But we're meeting like this.</i>

280
00:23:29,042 --> 00:23:31,458
<i>And I'm telling you how this goes.</i>

281
00:23:31,542 --> 00:23:34,333
<i>Now, keep your voice down
and do exactly as I say.</i>

282
00:23:34,417 --> 00:23:37,167
- And you're watching me right now?
<i>- Yes, I am.</i>

283
00:23:37,875 --> 00:23:39,000
And what am I doing?

284
00:23:40,000 --> 00:23:42,500
You should put that down
before Sarkowski sees it.

285
00:23:50,458 --> 00:23:51,958
I like this kid.

286
00:23:52,042 --> 00:23:53,667
<i>Okay. I found something.</i>

287
00:23:53,750 --> 00:23:56,750
<i>I've got a pay stub, girlfriend maybe.</i>

288
00:23:56,833 --> 00:23:58,250
<i>Sending it now.</i>

289
00:24:03,375 --> 00:24:05,958
Nora Parisi. Twenty-seven,

290
00:24:06,875 --> 00:24:10,125
recently promoted to manager
of Northwind Operations.

291
00:24:10,208 --> 00:24:12,542
<i>Wait. I found something else.</i>

292
00:24:15,500 --> 00:24:17,583
Listen, asshole.

293
00:24:19,083 --> 00:24:21,833
I work for
the Department of Homeland Security.

294
00:24:21,917 --> 00:24:25,125
<i>That's like the janitor at NASA</i>
<i>calling himself an astronaut.</i>

295
00:24:25,208 --> 00:24:26,958
<i>You're a low-level TSO,</i>

296
00:24:27,042 --> 00:24:29,625
<i>you're going nowhere,
and loving every minute of it.</i>

297
00:24:29,708 --> 00:24:31,250
He's putting a call through.

298
00:24:32,708 --> 00:24:35,417
<i></i><i>Hang up now or Nora dies.</i>

299
00:24:38,833 --> 00:24:40,292
What did you just say?

300
00:24:40,375 --> 00:24:43,125
<i>My people have
a Barrett M82 sniper rifle at her head.</i>

301
00:24:43,208 --> 00:24:44,292
<i>Hang up the call…</i>

302
00:24:44,375 --> 00:24:47,417
<i>- </i><i>911, what's your emergency?</i>
<i>- …Or we execute your girlfriend.</i>

303
00:24:50,125 --> 00:24:53,625
<i>Your pregnant girlfriend
over at Northwind Operations.</i>

304
00:24:53,708 --> 00:24:55,083
<i> Hello? Is anyone there?</i>

305
00:24:55,167 --> 00:24:57,333
<i>I told you this is how it goes.</i>

306
00:24:57,417 --> 00:24:58,500
<i>Hello?</i>

307
00:24:59,875 --> 00:25:00,875
<i>Hello?</i>

308
00:25:00,958 --> 00:25:03,083
<i>Get up and lock it</i>
<i>in the lost and found.</i>

309
00:25:03,167 --> 00:25:04,167
Okay.

310
00:25:17,417 --> 00:25:18,417
<i>I said lock it.</i>

311
00:25:18,500 --> 00:25:21,833
<i>The quicker you accept this,
Ethan, the safer you and Nora will be.</i>

312
00:25:21,917 --> 00:25:24,125
I accept it. Just be cool, okay?

313
00:25:27,000 --> 00:25:29,125
<i>Today won't be easy,</i>
<i>but it'll be simple.</i>

314
00:25:29,208 --> 00:25:32,542
<i>When the plane departs at 5:40,
you and Nora are free to live your lives.</i>

315
00:25:32,625 --> 00:25:36,208
<i>If the bag gets flagged, she dies.
If you talk to the police, she dies.</i>

316
00:25:36,292 --> 00:25:37,792
<i>If anyone opens the bag...</i>

317
00:25:37,875 --> 00:25:39,083
Okay. I get it.

318
00:25:39,167 --> 00:25:40,667
<i>Good because I'm watching.</i>

319
00:25:40,750 --> 00:25:43,583
<i>Now, you were a runner.
Pick a track, stay in your lane.</i>

320
00:25:43,667 --> 00:25:46,542
<i>You've never made waves before, Ethan.
You're not going to start now.</i>

321
00:25:46,625 --> 00:25:48,458
<i>One bag for one life.</i>

322
00:25:48,542 --> 00:25:51,458
<i>All you have to do is nothing.</i>

323
00:25:54,958 --> 00:25:58,292
<i>Congresswoman Grace Turner</i>
<i>still faces a significant challenge</i>

324
00:25:58,375 --> 00:26:01,708
<i>in acquiring the votes in Congress
for her DTD Bill.</i>

325
00:26:01,792 --> 00:26:05,500
<i> There's a vital conversation</i>
<i>we need to have about military spending</i>

326
00:26:05,583 --> 00:26:07,167
<i>particularly its role in defending…</i>

327
00:26:07,250 --> 00:26:08,167
What the hell?

328
00:26:08,250 --> 00:26:11,167
<i>It's a topic that touches the core
of our International responsibilities…</i>

329
00:26:11,250 --> 00:26:13,958
- Sorry.
<i>- …And national security.</i>

330
00:26:14,042 --> 00:26:15,667
Texting and driving.

331
00:26:17,667 --> 00:26:18,667
Sorry.

332
00:26:28,375 --> 00:26:29,917
What do you got, Detective?

333
00:26:30,542 --> 00:26:34,750
Olek Vedenyapin and his nephew
Yuri Balakin. Olek was Bratva.

334
00:26:34,833 --> 00:26:36,333
Yeah, he ran the port.

335
00:26:37,417 --> 00:26:41,042
We've been trying to connect him to that
double homicide on Hawthorne last year.

336
00:26:41,125 --> 00:26:43,125
Burn pattern suggests
some type of accelerant.

337
00:26:43,208 --> 00:26:45,125
Nephew was shot dead before the fire.

338
00:26:45,208 --> 00:26:46,625
Did you dig up a bullet yet?

339
00:26:49,625 --> 00:26:53,333
Hydra-Shok. Bougie. Same COD as Olek?

340
00:26:53,417 --> 00:26:56,458
We haven't found any other rounds.
ME will have to autopsy.

341
00:27:11,583 --> 00:27:12,708
It's a cricket.

342
00:27:13,417 --> 00:27:15,250
ATF bug. Standalone.

343
00:27:15,833 --> 00:27:18,417
Bugs that broadcast can be easily detected

344
00:27:18,500 --> 00:27:22,000
but this little guy
can record up to 72 hours.

345
00:27:22,083 --> 00:27:24,708
Too bad it's cooked.
It probably recorded the murder.

346
00:27:25,667 --> 00:27:28,000
I know somebody
who might be able to uncook it.

347
00:27:33,333 --> 00:27:36,250
Everyone, the TSA would like to
personally congratulate you

348
00:27:36,333 --> 00:27:38,000
for escaping the LA traffic.

349
00:27:38,083 --> 00:27:42,167
To facilitate your getaway safely,
we're gonna play a game I like to call…

350
00:27:42,250 --> 00:27:44,458
- Put it in a bin!
- Put it in a bin.

351
00:27:44,542 --> 00:27:46,292
I'm not going through that machine

352
00:27:46,375 --> 00:27:48,792
so you and your perv buddies
can take naked photos.

353
00:27:48,875 --> 00:27:50,708
They always do this.
I'm late for my flight.

354
00:27:50,792 --> 00:27:52,875
I have my student ID. Is that okay?

355
00:27:53,625 --> 00:27:55,458
- Do you have a passport?
- No.

356
00:27:55,542 --> 00:27:59,333
I will not bow to a repressive government
that wants to violate my human rights.

357
00:27:59,417 --> 00:28:02,000
Keys, wallets, personal items.

358
00:28:02,083 --> 00:28:03,083
Put it in a bin!

359
00:28:03,167 --> 00:28:05,351
- Is this 'cause I'm Muslim?
- Is this 'cause I'm Black?

360
00:28:05,375 --> 00:28:06,625
Is this 'cause I'm white?

361
00:28:06,708 --> 00:28:10,000
You're putting on a show down here
so the cameras up there can profile us.

362
00:28:10,083 --> 00:28:11,458
Do I look like a problem to you?

363
00:28:11,542 --> 00:28:13,792
Your granny's cupcakes,
your mom's sweet potato pie.

364
00:28:13,875 --> 00:28:15,667
Put it in the bin!

365
00:28:18,000 --> 00:28:19,500
Bingo. Pay up.

366
00:28:23,583 --> 00:28:25,708
<i>Hey, you seem very tense.</i>

367
00:28:27,000 --> 00:28:28,208
I wonder why.

368
00:28:28,292 --> 00:28:31,708
<i>Well, when travelers see guys like you
get tense, they get tense.</i>

369
00:28:31,792 --> 00:28:35,417
<i>And that's bad for me, which means
it's bad for Nora. Okay? So calm down.</i>

370
00:28:35,500 --> 00:28:38,458
You want me to be calm
with a gun pointed at my girlfriend.

371
00:28:38,542 --> 00:28:40,917
<i>Let's just try to put it
out of your mind. Okay?</i>

372
00:28:42,125 --> 00:28:43,875
<i>Tell me about your holiday plans.</i>

373
00:28:43,958 --> 00:28:45,125
Yeah, okay.

374
00:28:45,208 --> 00:28:46,708
<i>I'm not asking, Ethan.</i>

375
00:28:49,208 --> 00:28:50,458
We don't have any, okay?

376
00:28:50,542 --> 00:28:51,875
<i>You have no holiday plans?</i>

377
00:28:52,500 --> 00:28:55,000
<i>I sense maybe you're not
a fan of Christmas, right?</i>

378
00:28:55,083 --> 00:28:57,708
It's a holiday that makes
everyone feel they're not doing it right

379
00:28:57,792 --> 00:28:59,167
no matter what they do.

380
00:28:59,250 --> 00:29:04,333
They're never happy enough,
never rich enough, never enough enough.

381
00:29:04,417 --> 00:29:07,958
<i>Bah humbug.
To me, Christmas is all about family.</i>

382
00:29:08,042 --> 00:29:10,708
Really? The anonymous criminal
threatening my pregnant girlfriend's

383
00:29:10,792 --> 00:29:13,708
- telling me the meaning of Christmas?
<i>- That's a fair point.</i>

384
00:29:14,292 --> 00:29:16,125
<i>Tell me where you met, you and Nora.</i>

385
00:29:19,542 --> 00:29:20,375
Post office.

386
00:29:20,458 --> 00:29:23,542
<i>Well, that's cute. I thought
your generation only met on apps.</i>

387
00:29:23,625 --> 00:29:25,625
<i>Let me guess. She got a big job out west</i>

388
00:29:25,708 --> 00:29:29,000
<i>and you didn't have anything else going
except her so you came along for the ride.</i>

389
00:29:29,083 --> 00:29:32,167
<i>Now you got nothing else going on
in a whole new city.</i>

390
00:29:32,917 --> 00:29:35,917
<i>Passengers bound for Chicago</i>
<i>on Northwind Flight 827</i>

391
00:29:36,042 --> 00:29:38,042
<i>will be boarding soon at Gate 8.</i>

392
00:29:40,292 --> 00:29:42,958
<i>How do your parents like her?</i>
<i>They approve?</i>

393
00:29:44,750 --> 00:29:47,167
They haven't spent a lot of time with her.

394
00:29:49,792 --> 00:29:51,375
They live in Florida.

395
00:29:51,458 --> 00:29:54,042
<i>Hmm. Boy, that's nice.</i>

396
00:29:54,833 --> 00:29:57,208
Look…

397
00:29:59,208 --> 00:30:03,375
I am not trying to piss you off,
but this isn't helping.

398
00:30:04,750 --> 00:30:08,625
Nothing's going to take my mind off
the fact you're threatening my girlfriend.

399
00:30:08,708 --> 00:30:12,667
<i>Whatever you're trying to sneak
through security isn't going to work.</i>

400
00:30:12,750 --> 00:30:13,875
Naughty, naughty.

401
00:30:14,708 --> 00:30:15,792
They got dogs and...

402
00:30:15,875 --> 00:30:17,542
<i>Let's cancel the text.</i>

403
00:30:18,792 --> 00:30:21,417
<i>Reach down and cancel that text right now.</i>

404
00:30:23,417 --> 00:30:26,417
<i>Attaboy. Now, stand up
and walk over to the drawer</i>

405
00:30:26,500 --> 00:30:28,792
<i>and put the watch in there
next to your phone.</i>

406
00:30:32,000 --> 00:30:33,958
<i>We're off to a real bad start here.</i>

407
00:30:34,042 --> 00:30:36,583
<i>This won't work if I can't trust you.
Understand?</i>

408
00:30:36,667 --> 00:30:37,583
You can trust me.

409
00:30:37,667 --> 00:30:39,875
<i>You sure? 'Cause you've been
lying to me since we met.</i>

410
00:30:39,958 --> 00:30:42,167
<i>Your parents do not live in Florida.</i>

411
00:30:42,250 --> 00:30:44,333
<i>They moved back to the city six years ago</i>

412
00:30:44,417 --> 00:30:48,458
<i>and your father used to work in private
security at the Freehold Raceway Mall</i>

413
00:30:48,542 --> 00:30:51,458
<i>and your mother still teaches at PS 86.</i>

414
00:30:51,542 --> 00:30:52,750
Who the hell are you?

415
00:30:52,833 --> 00:30:54,250
<i>I'm the guy you listen to.</i>

416
00:30:54,333 --> 00:30:56,125
<i>Now, I've given you two warnings</i>

417
00:30:56,208 --> 00:30:58,917
<i>and the next time,
there's gonna be consequences.</i>

418
00:30:59,000 --> 00:31:00,500
<i>Do you understand me?</i>

419
00:31:01,083 --> 00:31:04,292
<i>Stop nodding and say it. "I understand."</i>

420
00:31:04,375 --> 00:31:05,667
I understand.

421
00:31:05,750 --> 00:31:08,750
<i>Good. My associate's on his way.</i>

422
00:31:10,542 --> 00:31:11,833
What's really in the bag?

423
00:31:11,917 --> 00:31:15,750
<i>It doesn't matter. The bag stays shut.</i>

424
00:31:17,750 --> 00:31:18,958
<i>Okay? Say that.</i>

425
00:31:20,292 --> 00:31:21,583
The bag stays shut.

426
00:31:22,667 --> 00:31:25,500
You know how many Targets
I had to go to to get these?

427
00:31:25,583 --> 00:31:28,417
This is extortion, felony offense.
You'd do three years.

428
00:31:28,500 --> 00:31:32,958
Well, you wanted a rush on your cricket
and I wanted peppermint Ho Hos.

429
00:31:34,042 --> 00:31:35,167
They're delicious

430
00:31:35,750 --> 00:31:37,875
and Shira won't buy Christmas flavors.

431
00:31:37,958 --> 00:31:39,125
Mmm-hmm.

432
00:31:47,250 --> 00:31:49,875
Oh, my gosh. That is so good.

433
00:31:50,583 --> 00:31:54,042
I'm usually the only one here
on Christmas Eve. Get caught up.

434
00:31:54,125 --> 00:31:56,625
- Shouldn't you be with family?
- Dinner's at 5:00.

435
00:31:56,708 --> 00:31:59,000
Or 4:00, whatev…
What's up with the cricket?

436
00:31:59,583 --> 00:32:00,583
You were right.

437
00:32:00,667 --> 00:32:02,833
ATF's been surveilling this guy
for a while.

438
00:32:02,917 --> 00:32:06,125
Mostly sells arms to Russians.
You think they're behind this?

439
00:32:06,208 --> 00:32:07,333
Could be.

440
00:32:07,417 --> 00:32:08,625
But something feels off.

441
00:32:09,333 --> 00:32:11,917
Olek's been steady for years,
reliable for them.

442
00:32:12,625 --> 00:32:14,792
Why would his Russian buddies
kill him now?

443
00:32:15,625 --> 00:32:17,167
You got anything off the bug?

444
00:32:17,250 --> 00:32:20,958
Not much. I took what I could restore,
isolated highs and lows.

445
00:32:21,542 --> 00:32:22,750
Here's what I got.

446
00:32:34,417 --> 00:32:35,625
<i>Merry Christmas.</i>

447
00:32:36,500 --> 00:32:37,500
That's it.

448
00:32:40,667 --> 00:32:42,333
You don't deserve Ho Hos.

449
00:32:42,417 --> 00:32:44,500
It was in a fire.

450
00:32:44,583 --> 00:32:46,458
This is a Christmas miracle.

451
00:32:47,292 --> 00:32:48,292
Hallelujah.

452
00:32:56,792 --> 00:32:58,542
You said you have a family?

453
00:32:58,625 --> 00:33:01,000
<i>No,</i>
<i>I said Christmas is about family.</i>

454
00:33:01,083 --> 00:33:04,292
<i>- But I do have a son.</i>
- Does he know what you do for a living?

455
00:33:04,375 --> 00:33:06,292
<i>He thinks I'm in insurance.</i>

456
00:33:06,375 --> 00:33:09,042
<i>But that's not what
you really want to ask, is it?</i>

457
00:33:12,458 --> 00:33:13,458
Are you a terrorist?

458
00:33:13,542 --> 00:33:14,833
<i>No, Ethan, I'm not.</i>

459
00:33:14,917 --> 00:33:18,208
<i>I consider myself
more of a freelance facilitator. Okay?</i>

460
00:33:18,292 --> 00:33:19,375
What does that mean?

461
00:33:19,458 --> 00:33:21,833
<i>Clients hire me
to facilitate a specific result.</i>

462
00:33:21,917 --> 00:33:23,250
<i>It varies from job to job.</i>

463
00:33:23,333 --> 00:33:25,333
And what's the result you're after now?

464
00:33:25,417 --> 00:33:27,042
<i>Get a bag on a plane.</i>

465
00:33:28,708 --> 00:33:29,542
Right.

466
00:33:29,625 --> 00:33:30,458
<i>What about you?</i>

467
00:33:30,542 --> 00:33:33,625
<i>You've been on autopilot
for a while now. Why don't you quit?</i>

468
00:33:33,708 --> 00:33:34,958
I will if you will.

469
00:33:35,042 --> 00:33:38,792
<i>No, I'm serious. A smart guy like you
had to have aspirations at some point.</i>

470
00:33:38,875 --> 00:33:41,208
<i>What'd you have pinned up
on that vision board?</i>

471
00:33:41,292 --> 00:33:45,042
Well, you're the one who knows everything.
Why don't you tell me? Huh?

472
00:33:45,792 --> 00:33:46,625
<i>All right.</i>

473
00:33:46,708 --> 00:33:49,458
<i>You're a son of a security guard,
you're observant.</i>

474
00:33:49,542 --> 00:33:51,000
<i>How about… cop?</i>

475
00:33:53,875 --> 00:33:55,083
<i>I'm right, aren't I?</i>

476
00:33:55,958 --> 00:33:57,583
<i>Yeah, tell me what happened.</i>

477
00:33:59,375 --> 00:34:00,792
I didn't make the cut.

478
00:34:00,875 --> 00:34:03,000
They kicked me out right before placement.

479
00:34:03,500 --> 00:34:05,833
<i>Oh. Why would they
go and do a thing like that?</i>

480
00:34:05,917 --> 00:34:07,184
<i>- What'd you do?</i>
- Next question.

481
00:34:07,208 --> 00:34:09,583
<i>A nerve hit. Okay.</i>

482
00:34:09,667 --> 00:34:11,875
<i>You tell me when you're ready.
Was that it?</i>

483
00:34:11,958 --> 00:34:15,042
<i>Did you ever reapply
or is that a touchy story too?</i>

484
00:34:16,750 --> 00:34:18,500
My dad wanted to be a cop.

485
00:34:18,583 --> 00:34:21,292
Applied so many times
they flat out stopped responding.

486
00:34:23,750 --> 00:34:26,375
You know what he does now?
Of course you do.

487
00:34:26,458 --> 00:34:27,875
<i>He drives an Uber.</i>

488
00:34:28,667 --> 00:34:29,583
Yeah.

489
00:34:29,667 --> 00:34:33,000
<i>So the world kicks him down,
you lie down next to him. Why is that?</i>

490
00:34:33,083 --> 00:34:34,917
Dreams have an expiration date.

491
00:34:36,792 --> 00:34:39,625
<i>I bet it's started to
eat at your relationship with Nora.</i>

492
00:34:39,708 --> 00:34:42,292
<i>I bet she loves all the cynicism.</i>

493
00:34:42,375 --> 00:34:44,500
She has a different outlook.

494
00:34:44,583 --> 00:34:46,250
<i>I'm not saying chase your dreams.</i>

495
00:34:46,333 --> 00:34:48,493
<i>That's not a very honest thing to say…</i>

496
00:34:48,542 --> 00:34:51,917
<i>…but there is no need to hate
every minute of waking life.</i>

497
00:34:52,000 --> 00:34:54,000
<i>Your generation is just so taken</i>

498
00:34:54,083 --> 00:34:56,625
<i>with the concept of authenticity…</i>

499
00:34:56,708 --> 00:34:58,625
<i>…that you will not take a bite</i>

500
00:34:58,708 --> 00:35:01,750
<i>unless you know
it's the perfect hashtag real thing.</i>

501
00:35:02,333 --> 00:35:05,833
<i>Real coffee, real pizza, real bagel.</i>

502
00:35:05,917 --> 00:35:09,667
<i>The thing you kids haven't
come around to is that there's no real.</i>

503
00:35:09,750 --> 00:35:13,542
<i>Fulfillment is a lie
that they use to sell paper towels.</i>

504
00:35:13,625 --> 00:35:14,792
Hey, now who's cynical?

505
00:35:14,875 --> 00:35:17,458
<i>No, I'm just experienced enough
to know life's disappointing,</i>

506
00:35:17,542 --> 00:35:19,333
<i>and it's short and if you're smart,</i>

507
00:35:19,417 --> 00:35:22,000
<i>you can steal
what happiness you can when you can.</i>

508
00:35:22,083 --> 00:35:25,167
<i>Or just stay on autopilot
the rest of your life. Your call.</i>

509
00:35:37,500 --> 00:35:40,917
<i>You know, the lucky ones find a job
that pays the most money…</i>

510
00:35:42,167 --> 00:35:43,708
<i>…for the least amount of work.</i>

511
00:35:45,125 --> 00:35:48,583
<i>And they spend the rest of their time
doing whatever makes them happy.</i>

512
00:35:52,417 --> 00:35:53,417
Like you.

513
00:35:54,292 --> 00:35:57,083
You'd be surprised
how well I live.

514
00:35:58,583 --> 00:36:01,625
Does it take a doctorate
to read a computer screen? Let's go.

515
00:36:04,750 --> 00:36:07,458
- I need a LEO on four. Bag check.
- This is unreal.

516
00:36:11,125 --> 00:36:14,458
It's called a book. You might read one
when you get your GED.

517
00:36:14,542 --> 00:36:16,667
Buddy, relax. Let the guy work.

518
00:36:16,750 --> 00:36:19,292
Sir, could I see
your boarding pass, please?

519
00:36:20,875 --> 00:36:23,292
Mr. Herter, I need to conduct
a quick inspection.

520
00:36:23,375 --> 00:36:25,375
If you prefer,
we can use a private room.

521
00:36:25,458 --> 00:36:27,542
No, do it here.
I'm already late to board.

522
00:36:27,625 --> 00:36:30,292
In that case,
I'll have a law enforcement officer

523
00:36:30,375 --> 00:36:33,375
run your boarding pass while I search.

524
00:36:35,625 --> 00:36:36,792
It'll save time.

525
00:36:36,875 --> 00:36:38,500
I don't think this is necessary.

526
00:36:38,583 --> 00:36:40,750
New fraud alert from SFO.

527
00:36:41,750 --> 00:36:42,750
Yeah.

528
00:36:59,292 --> 00:37:00,292
Okay.

529
00:37:01,083 --> 00:37:04,292
You're all clear.
Probably just an imaging glitch.

530
00:37:05,083 --> 00:37:07,208
You TSA guys are a joke.

531
00:37:08,250 --> 00:37:11,000
- You know that, right?
- Thank you for your patience.

532
00:37:11,917 --> 00:37:14,250
You can wait over there
for your boarding pass.

533
00:37:19,417 --> 00:37:22,375
<i>There's a story I once heard</i>
<i>about a tribe in the Serengeti.</i>

534
00:37:25,667 --> 00:37:27,208
<i>Every summer when the game was sparse,</i>

535
00:37:27,292 --> 00:37:30,042
<i>the tribe would depend on a single
apple tree for most of its food.</i>

536
00:37:30,125 --> 00:37:33,292
<i>Then one day they learned
that the tree had been plucked bare.</i>

537
00:37:33,375 --> 00:37:36,250
<i>The apples had been stolen
by one of their own.</i>

538
00:37:37,083 --> 00:37:38,583
<i>"I'm sorry," the thief pled.</i>

539
00:37:38,667 --> 00:37:41,583
<i>"I needed those apples
to feed my children."</i>

540
00:37:41,667 --> 00:37:46,250
<i>The tribe forgave him and made do
until the tree bore fruit once more.</i>

541
00:37:46,333 --> 00:37:49,542
<i>They returned, and lo and behold,
what'd they see?</i>

542
00:37:50,208 --> 00:37:53,125
<i>The apples were gone again.
Pilfered by the same thief.</i>

543
00:37:54,167 --> 00:37:55,667
<i>"I'm sorry," the thief begged.</i>

544
00:37:55,750 --> 00:37:57,917
<i>"I needed those apples
to feed my children."</i>

545
00:37:58,583 --> 00:38:02,167
<i>Even though the tribe was
without food yet again, they forgave him.</i>

546
00:38:03,083 --> 00:38:05,292
<i>When the apples grew back,</i>

547
00:38:05,375 --> 00:38:08,708
<i>the tribe's elders knew
the thief would return.</i>

548
00:38:08,792 --> 00:38:09,792
<i>Excuse me.</i>

549
00:38:14,500 --> 00:38:16,667
<i>So, when night fell,</i>

550
00:38:17,458 --> 00:38:19,375
<i>they crept into the man's hut</i>

551
00:38:19,458 --> 00:38:21,667
<i>and slit the throats
of all three children.</i>

552
00:38:23,417 --> 00:38:25,417
<i>You want to know why, Ethan?</i>

553
00:38:29,000 --> 00:38:32,417
<i>Because they learned that there can be
no lesson without consequence.</i>

554
00:38:35,792 --> 00:38:37,500
Somebody call a doctor!

555
00:38:41,333 --> 00:38:43,458
- Call a paramedic!
- Get a doctor!

556
00:38:43,542 --> 00:38:44,583
Officer down.

557
00:38:44,667 --> 00:38:46,708
Back up! Everybody, back up!

558
00:38:46,792 --> 00:38:47,833
Back up!

559
00:38:55,625 --> 00:38:56,792
Hey, Nora.

560
00:38:56,875 --> 00:38:59,500
Did you hear about the officer
at the TSO checkpoint?

561
00:38:59,583 --> 00:39:00,875
- Yeah.
- Oh, my God.

562
00:39:00,958 --> 00:39:02,625
Lionel. Sweet man.

563
00:39:02,708 --> 00:39:03,958
I'm so sorry.

564
00:39:04,042 --> 00:39:07,333
I've been trying to get a hold of Ethan.
He was with the guy.

565
00:39:07,417 --> 00:39:09,875
- I don't know why he's not picking up.
- Go for it.

566
00:39:22,917 --> 00:39:25,250
He was a friend of yours,
wasn't he?

567
00:39:28,458 --> 00:39:29,542
It's a shame.

568
00:39:29,625 --> 00:39:32,500
Family man like that
having a heart attack.

569
00:39:34,167 --> 00:39:35,167
You killed him.

570
00:39:35,792 --> 00:39:38,458
I don't know about that.
I gave you some simple rules.

571
00:39:38,542 --> 00:39:40,958
You got cute. I'd say you killed him.

572
00:39:42,792 --> 00:39:44,667
You feel like killing someone else?

573
00:39:47,250 --> 00:39:48,250
Nora?

574
00:39:54,083 --> 00:39:55,083
I told you.

575
00:39:57,208 --> 00:40:00,292
I'm not some cartoon villain.
I'm just a regular guy like you

576
00:40:00,375 --> 00:40:04,292
except with goals
and a clear plan to achieve them.

577
00:40:04,375 --> 00:40:05,375
You, I see,

578
00:40:06,250 --> 00:40:08,000
like to improvise.

579
00:40:08,083 --> 00:40:12,417
"Active threat, not drugs, get Nora out,

580
00:40:12,500 --> 00:40:14,792
find smuggler near bar arcade."

581
00:40:14,875 --> 00:40:17,417
"Caucasian from New Jersey."

582
00:40:17,500 --> 00:40:19,625
That's good. How'd you get all that?

583
00:40:21,042 --> 00:40:24,917
You weren't worried about the dogs.
Whatever you're smuggling, it's not drugs.

584
00:40:25,917 --> 00:40:29,083
Bagel, pizza references
and you call Manhattan "the city".

585
00:40:29,417 --> 00:40:30,417
Hmm.

586
00:40:30,792 --> 00:40:34,625
Only people from New York
or Jersey call it that.

587
00:40:36,083 --> 00:40:38,583
Kept saying we're a lot alike.
I took a shot.

588
00:40:38,667 --> 00:40:42,500
Plus, I've played <i>Area 51</i>
every day for two years.

589
00:40:42,583 --> 00:40:44,417
I know that sound in my sleep.

590
00:40:45,000 --> 00:40:46,833
You said I wasn't your first choice.

591
00:40:47,417 --> 00:40:49,167
Supposed to be Jason, wasn't it?

592
00:40:49,250 --> 00:40:50,250
Yep.

593
00:40:51,625 --> 00:40:53,625
His twins are three.

594
00:40:56,625 --> 00:40:57,625
You would have…

595
00:41:00,292 --> 00:41:02,292
That would have been up to Jason.

596
00:41:02,375 --> 00:41:05,292
But if I had to, without hesitation.

597
00:41:05,375 --> 00:41:07,000
That's what you're dealing with.

598
00:41:07,083 --> 00:41:10,167
I want you to think about that,
and I want you to think about Nora.

599
00:41:11,417 --> 00:41:13,250
Then I want you to stop thinking.

600
00:41:18,458 --> 00:41:20,375
Now, this is the way the world works.

601
00:41:20,458 --> 00:41:22,083
There's people in control

602
00:41:22,792 --> 00:41:24,625
and there's people that listen.

603
00:41:26,042 --> 00:41:27,250
You listening?

604
00:41:29,958 --> 00:41:31,417
Ethan, are you listening?

605
00:41:31,500 --> 00:41:32,500
Yeah.

606
00:41:34,417 --> 00:41:36,750
In a few minutes,
a guy with a red baseball cap

607
00:41:36,833 --> 00:41:38,667
is gonna walk into your lane.

608
00:41:38,750 --> 00:41:40,208
What do you have to do?

609
00:41:41,958 --> 00:41:43,042
Nothing.

610
00:41:44,375 --> 00:41:45,375
That's right.

611
00:41:51,375 --> 00:41:53,875
Tell me there isn't something horrible
in that bag.

612
00:41:55,250 --> 00:41:56,250
No.

613
00:42:16,958 --> 00:42:18,042
Lionel.

614
00:42:20,792 --> 00:42:23,125
It's messed up, man. You okay?

615
00:42:24,417 --> 00:42:25,417
Yeah.

616
00:42:25,500 --> 00:42:29,125
Nora called me, like, three times
trying to reach you. Call her back yet?

617
00:42:29,792 --> 00:42:33,458
I will, thanks.
And thanks for covering for me.

618
00:42:36,500 --> 00:42:37,500
I got it now.

619
00:42:39,750 --> 00:42:40,958
It's all right, man.

620
00:42:42,500 --> 00:42:45,708
Hey. Uh, you benching me?

621
00:42:45,792 --> 00:42:47,792
No, putting you back on metal detectors.

622
00:42:48,417 --> 00:42:50,375
Lionel's passing, this place is packed.

623
00:42:50,458 --> 00:42:52,958
Today is not the day to experiment.
I'll give you another shot.

624
00:42:53,042 --> 00:42:55,042
We'll talk about your future later.
But right now,

625
00:42:55,125 --> 00:42:57,333
Jason's back on the machine
and that's final.

626
00:42:58,500 --> 00:43:01,417
<i>If you're not on that machine</i>
<i>by the time our man gets there,</i>

627
00:43:01,500 --> 00:43:02,417
<i>you're in breach.</i>

628
00:43:02,500 --> 00:43:04,292
<i>Then maybe I don't start with Nora.</i>

629
00:43:04,375 --> 00:43:06,292
Yeah, I don't care what you do to me.

630
00:43:06,375 --> 00:43:07,792
<i>Who said anything about you?</i>

631
00:43:09,500 --> 00:43:11,667
<i>Your friend there
is coming off the machine.</i>

632
00:43:11,750 --> 00:43:14,042
<i>You can decide
if it happens your way or mine.</i>

633
00:43:15,333 --> 00:43:16,333
Look, I…

634
00:43:16,958 --> 00:43:20,208
My supervisor reassigned me.
What do you want me to do?

635
00:43:20,875 --> 00:43:22,958
<i>You're a smart kid, you'll figure it out.</i>

636
00:44:28,833 --> 00:44:30,542
<i>Whatever you're doing, do it fast.</i>

637
00:44:30,625 --> 00:44:32,000
Not helping.

638
00:44:38,125 --> 00:44:40,667
Hey, Ethan, I wanted to check on you.

639
00:44:40,750 --> 00:44:43,500
What happened to Lionel,
it's tragic, so sad.

640
00:44:43,583 --> 00:44:45,125
Yeah. I know.

641
00:44:45,208 --> 00:44:47,917
I thought we could start
a GoFundMe for his family.

642
00:44:48,000 --> 00:44:51,042
His wife and kids
I'm sure could use the help. Yeah?

643
00:44:51,708 --> 00:44:53,250
Yeah. Yeah, I'm in.

644
00:44:54,625 --> 00:44:58,125
You know, I think I heard
Samir talking about the same thing.

645
00:44:58,208 --> 00:45:00,333
- You should hit him up. Join forces.
- Yeah.

646
00:45:00,417 --> 00:45:01,500
Good idea.

647
00:45:15,917 --> 00:45:17,083
What's up, man?

648
00:45:17,167 --> 00:45:20,250
I think I left my phone
down the side there.

649
00:45:20,333 --> 00:45:22,208
Do you see it? Down the bottom.

650
00:45:25,250 --> 00:45:26,750
- There's nothing there.
- No?

651
00:45:26,833 --> 00:45:29,167
Ah, I put it in the lost and found.

652
00:45:30,083 --> 00:45:32,917
- You okay?
- Sorry. Yeah, just a bit out of it today.

653
00:45:33,708 --> 00:45:35,917
<i>That's not bad. Allow me.</i>

654
00:46:00,083 --> 00:46:01,708
Step forward please, sir.

655
00:46:03,542 --> 00:46:06,042
All right, hold the line. Hold the line.

656
00:46:06,667 --> 00:46:09,083
Raise your arms for me please.

657
00:46:13,875 --> 00:46:15,375
Man, really?

658
00:46:17,458 --> 00:46:19,083
Turn around for me please, sir.

659
00:46:20,792 --> 00:46:21,792
This isn't mine.

660
00:46:21,875 --> 00:46:24,116
- People's safety depends on you.
- I said it's not mine.

661
00:46:24,667 --> 00:46:26,958
I don't care what problems you have.
Don't bring 'em here.

662
00:46:27,042 --> 00:46:29,042
- It's not...
- Let's go. You're going home.

663
00:46:32,750 --> 00:46:34,125
Ethan, you're back on four.

664
00:46:35,458 --> 00:46:37,625
- Why? What's going on?
- Just do it.

665
00:46:41,708 --> 00:46:43,417
<i>Hey, you did good.</i>

666
00:46:43,500 --> 00:46:44,500
Go to hell.

667
00:46:45,542 --> 00:46:47,042
I didn't say anything.

668
00:46:59,708 --> 00:47:01,333
You know, it's pretty weird.

669
00:47:02,250 --> 00:47:03,250
What?

670
00:47:03,917 --> 00:47:06,958
How your buddy, who's our
designated driver every bar night,

671
00:47:07,042 --> 00:47:09,333
gets himself fired
for drinking on the job.

672
00:47:11,917 --> 00:47:13,542
I thought I met assholes before…

673
00:47:14,500 --> 00:47:16,625
<i>Okay, Ethan,</i>
<i>it's time to save Nora's life.</i>

674
00:47:16,708 --> 00:47:19,542
<i>Red baseball cap,
three o'clock, by the bins.</i>

675
00:47:19,625 --> 00:47:20,625
<i>That's our guy.</i>

676
00:47:40,833 --> 00:47:42,042
<i>Nov… chuck.</i>

677
00:49:37,417 --> 00:49:38,917
Yeah. Get me Homeland.

678
00:49:50,875 --> 00:49:51,875
Hey!

679
00:49:54,042 --> 00:49:55,250
<i>Ethan.</i>

680
00:50:08,750 --> 00:50:09,958
Thank you.

681
00:50:11,792 --> 00:50:12,917
<i>Let him go.</i>

682
00:50:22,750 --> 00:50:23,833
<i>Proud of you.</i>

683
00:50:28,083 --> 00:50:30,875
Asset says the locals
put out a call to Homeland.

684
00:50:31,708 --> 00:50:35,375
<i>That's fine. This is why</i>
<i>we have options. Where's the kid?</i>

685
00:50:39,167 --> 00:50:41,750
<i>Last call for Flight 1237…</i>

686
00:50:52,500 --> 00:50:54,875
There are 250 people on that flight.

687
00:50:56,000 --> 00:50:58,750
- You gonna kill 250 people?
- Mmm-hmm.

688
00:50:59,500 --> 00:51:01,708
I thought you said
you weren't a terrorist.

689
00:51:01,792 --> 00:51:06,208
I'm not. Terrorists kill for religious
or political or social objectives.

690
00:51:07,583 --> 00:51:09,417
Then why are you doing this?

691
00:51:09,500 --> 00:51:11,292
I'm not the doer either, Ethan.

692
00:51:11,375 --> 00:51:13,667
I'm just the one
that makes sure it gets done.

693
00:51:14,875 --> 00:51:16,083
Then I get paid.

694
00:51:16,167 --> 00:51:19,333
We're trained to identify explosives.
I've never seen anything like that.

695
00:51:19,417 --> 00:51:22,417
Well, it's an A 234 nerve agent
called Novichok 7.

696
00:51:22,500 --> 00:51:26,500
Causes instant cholinergic crisis,
followed by massive internal bleeding.

697
00:51:26,583 --> 00:51:30,000
Russians love it.
Body breaks down, organ by organ,

698
00:51:30,083 --> 00:51:32,875
until eventually you drown
in your own blood.

699
00:51:32,958 --> 00:51:36,542
I'll take that phone, by the way.
Just put it right here on the counter.

700
00:51:42,458 --> 00:51:43,667
Thank you.

701
00:51:44,583 --> 00:51:46,083
There are kids on that flight.

702
00:51:47,292 --> 00:51:51,125
Yeah. The people paying me
want to send a message.

703
00:51:52,125 --> 00:51:54,250
One a busy world will have to hear.

704
00:51:54,333 --> 00:51:56,583
What message? Who's paying you?

705
00:52:00,750 --> 00:52:02,250
Ethan, the bigger the job is,

706
00:52:02,333 --> 00:52:04,958
the fewer people there are
that can do it, okay?

707
00:52:05,042 --> 00:52:08,125
And there are jobs happening all around

708
00:52:08,208 --> 00:52:11,792
that most people can't see
and they all have casualties.

709
00:52:11,875 --> 00:52:15,458
Fortunately, I'm the guy who can keep
those casualties to a minimum.

710
00:52:15,542 --> 00:52:17,375
250 people is a minimum?

711
00:52:17,458 --> 00:52:19,292
There are much larger numbers.

712
00:52:19,375 --> 00:52:22,125
Why make me an accomplice?
Why not just check the bag?

713
00:52:22,208 --> 00:52:25,333
Every checked bag is sorted through
automated CTX machines, you know that.

714
00:52:25,417 --> 00:52:27,042
Our best odds are with carry-on.

715
00:52:27,125 --> 00:52:30,167
We just needed a little fix
at the machine. Thank you.

716
00:52:31,208 --> 00:52:33,958
Okay. It's through the machine.
You got what you wanted.

717
00:52:35,000 --> 00:52:36,083
You can let us go.

718
00:52:36,167 --> 00:52:38,125
Soon as that plane takes off.

719
00:52:47,292 --> 00:52:52,333
Look, the hard part's already over.
A couple hours, you'll get your life back,

720
00:52:52,417 --> 00:52:54,333
Nora's gonna be safe. You do love her?

721
00:52:54,417 --> 00:52:56,417
Yeah, of course I love her.

722
00:52:56,500 --> 00:52:58,083
Yeah? A lot of people say that.

723
00:52:58,167 --> 00:53:00,583
I'm giving you
the opportunity to prove it.

724
00:53:00,667 --> 00:53:02,583
Here's some gum. You want any?

725
00:53:05,958 --> 00:53:09,583
Now, your shift's lunch break
is coming up. What are you gonna do?

726
00:53:09,667 --> 00:53:11,333
I usually eat with Nora.

727
00:53:12,000 --> 00:53:14,250
Great. I was hoping to get to know Nora.

728
00:53:14,333 --> 00:53:18,250
Chew that gum, take her out to lunch.
I'll be listening. You guys brown-bag it?

729
00:53:18,333 --> 00:53:21,750
No. Wait. I can't. I can't just sit
and act like everything's normal.

730
00:53:21,833 --> 00:53:23,042
- It won't work...
- Ethan.

731
00:53:23,125 --> 00:53:25,500
You break routine, you attract attention.

732
00:53:26,292 --> 00:53:27,292
Almost done.

733
00:53:40,042 --> 00:53:44,292
Agent John Alcott, DHS.
I'm looking for a Detective Cole.

734
00:53:44,917 --> 00:53:47,167
- Down the hall on the left.
- Happy holidays.

735
00:53:47,250 --> 00:53:49,417
<i>You called Homeland</i>
<i>behind my back?</i>

736
00:53:49,500 --> 00:53:52,500
We're dealing with a potential
live threat. I made a judgment call.

737
00:53:52,583 --> 00:53:57,125
Oh, by all means. Let's involve federal
agencies based on potential threats.

738
00:53:57,208 --> 00:53:59,583
Elena, it's Christmas Eve. Go home.

739
00:53:59,667 --> 00:54:02,333
Excuse me, since she already called,
I'm already here,

740
00:54:02,417 --> 00:54:04,083
and I don't want to make the drive twice.

741
00:54:04,167 --> 00:54:07,000
We take every threat seriously,
but your captain's right.

742
00:54:07,083 --> 00:54:09,792
We cannot declare martial law
over a soft lead.

743
00:54:09,875 --> 00:54:11,500
And how is this a soft lead?

744
00:54:11,583 --> 00:54:14,500
An old-school Bratva underboss

745
00:54:14,583 --> 00:54:18,667
maybe says the word Novichok
on a damaged ATF wiretap. I mean, come on.

746
00:54:18,750 --> 00:54:20,542
Has there been
any chatter about an attack?

747
00:54:20,625 --> 00:54:22,500
Always, but there's nothing credible.

748
00:54:22,583 --> 00:54:25,250
There's no talk
about chemical weapons in Los Angeles.

749
00:54:25,333 --> 00:54:29,250
Elena, you're reaching. Now, I'm going
home to enjoy dinner with my family.

750
00:54:29,333 --> 00:54:31,667
- I suggest you do the same.
- Cap!

751
00:54:34,542 --> 00:54:36,083
Hey, you know what?

752
00:54:36,167 --> 00:54:39,042
Let me call my guy
at the Office of Bioweapons Affairs,

753
00:54:39,125 --> 00:54:41,625
but I'm telling you,
he's gonna say the same thing.

754
00:54:41,708 --> 00:54:46,375
EMS had a 911 call placed at 10:04
this morning from inside LAX.

755
00:54:46,458 --> 00:54:50,500
Line is registered to a TSA officer,
guy named Ethan Kopek.

756
00:54:50,583 --> 00:54:51,625
Told you.

757
00:54:58,750 --> 00:55:02,042
<i>I mean, Jason doesn't even</i>
<i>drink anymore. Like, ever.</i>

758
00:55:04,417 --> 00:55:05,875
Not since they had kids.

759
00:55:05,958 --> 00:55:08,458
Rochelle would have told me
if he needed help.

760
00:55:08,542 --> 00:55:10,250
Or I thought she would.

761
00:55:11,417 --> 00:55:13,250
Maybe Lionel dying just…

762
00:55:15,500 --> 00:55:17,875
- hit him hard.
- Oh. Mmm.

763
00:55:20,417 --> 00:55:22,875
You know, we should actually go to Tahiti.

764
00:55:24,000 --> 00:55:25,917
Never wait to celebrate, right?

765
00:55:27,708 --> 00:55:29,875
<i> Get more attentive, buddy.</i>

766
00:55:29,958 --> 00:55:32,083
You know, I wish we were there right now.

767
00:55:33,125 --> 00:55:35,750
So, tell me.

768
00:55:37,208 --> 00:55:38,417
What was your news?

769
00:55:39,167 --> 00:55:41,208
I… It doesn't matter.

770
00:55:41,292 --> 00:55:42,500
Of course it does.

771
00:55:43,458 --> 00:55:44,458
Tell me.

772
00:55:45,833 --> 00:55:48,250
<i>Normal, Ethan. Keep it normal.</i>

773
00:55:49,917 --> 00:55:52,625
So I went to speak to Sarkowski.

774
00:55:53,500 --> 00:55:55,750
About a promotion.

775
00:55:57,583 --> 00:55:59,708
And he's going to give me a trial run.

776
00:56:01,042 --> 00:56:04,583
Okay. And would that make you happy?

777
00:56:05,750 --> 00:56:09,458
Well, I just thought, you know,
we're going to need things.

778
00:56:10,667 --> 00:56:15,458
Doctors, car seats, cribs, clothes,
and, you know, those things cost money so…

779
00:56:15,542 --> 00:56:17,667
Well, we can figure out money.

780
00:56:19,833 --> 00:56:22,625
I only brought up the academy
because it was your dream.

781
00:56:23,625 --> 00:56:25,125
It was what you always wanted.

782
00:56:25,208 --> 00:56:27,625
Well, what if I don't know
what I want anymore?

783
00:56:27,708 --> 00:56:32,500
- <i>That is just sad.</i>
- Well, then we'll figure it out… together.

784
00:56:32,583 --> 00:56:33,417
Yeah.

785
00:56:33,500 --> 00:56:36,458
<i>Not the reaction</i>
<i>you were hoping for, huh, buddy?</i>

786
00:56:37,375 --> 00:56:39,208
I thought this was good news.

787
00:56:46,125 --> 00:56:49,250
What would you tell our kid
if they got knocked down?

788
00:56:50,375 --> 00:56:51,750
<i>Oh, that's good.</i>

789
00:56:51,833 --> 00:56:53,542
You'd say, "Give it another shot."

790
00:56:55,458 --> 00:56:56,875
Don't be afraid to fail.

791
00:56:56,958 --> 00:56:59,292
<i>That's a smart woman.</i>
<i>You should listen to her.</i>

792
00:56:59,375 --> 00:57:01,208
<i>Tell her she's right. Go on.</i>

793
00:57:02,208 --> 00:57:04,042
<i>- Tell her.</i>
- Take a risk, Ethan.

794
00:57:04,125 --> 00:57:06,750
<i>- Tell her.</i>
- Stop telling me what to do.

795
00:57:08,000 --> 00:57:10,875
<i>Oopsie-daisy.</i>
<i>Hope you got her a good present.</i>

796
00:57:10,958 --> 00:57:13,917
Hey, I… Hey, I'm… I'm sorry.

797
00:57:14,000 --> 00:57:16,417
That was too much.
You're just trying to help me.

798
00:57:16,500 --> 00:57:20,250
Forget it. It's fine.
It's been a really hard day.

799
00:57:21,958 --> 00:57:23,208
Yeah.

800
00:57:23,292 --> 00:57:25,833
- We can just talk tonight, okay?
- Okay.

801
00:57:26,458 --> 00:57:31,625
I, um… I gotta get back,
but call me end of shift.

802
00:57:32,500 --> 00:57:34,667
<i>Oh, you're gonna need
a big couch to sleep on tonight.</i>

803
00:57:34,750 --> 00:57:36,375
- Shut up.
<i>- Well, I'm just saying.</i>

804
00:57:36,458 --> 00:57:37,792
Hi, beautiful girl.

805
00:57:39,542 --> 00:57:41,958
- Merry Christmas.
- Merry Christmas.

806
00:57:44,333 --> 00:57:45,542
Nora?

807
00:57:49,208 --> 00:57:50,958
You're the best thing in my life.

808
00:57:53,500 --> 00:57:54,792
You too.

809
00:57:54,875 --> 00:57:56,500
<i>Hey, you're back in the bed.</i>

810
00:58:02,250 --> 00:58:04,042
No one ran this down?

811
00:58:04,125 --> 00:58:07,458
They did. Kopek's phone was off,
so they called LAXPD

812
00:58:07,542 --> 00:58:10,667
and an Officer Lionel Williams
gave the all clear.

813
00:58:10,750 --> 00:58:12,375
So it was logged as an error.

814
00:58:12,458 --> 00:58:15,667
Officer Williams died
less than two hours ago. Heart attack.

815
00:58:15,750 --> 00:58:19,125
- You don't buy it?
- And you do? Too many things.

816
00:58:19,208 --> 00:58:23,042
- That's not a category of threat.
- What 30-year-old turns off his phone?

817
00:58:25,083 --> 00:58:26,417
I need to talk to Kopek.

818
00:58:26,500 --> 00:58:28,042
Okay, I'll go with you.

819
00:58:28,125 --> 00:58:29,500
Thought it was a soft lead.

820
00:58:29,583 --> 00:58:32,375
Spirit of Christmas.
Plus, I can call my guy on the way.

821
00:58:32,458 --> 00:58:34,500
Rush order a tox screen
on Officer Williams.

822
00:58:34,583 --> 00:58:37,458
Let's put an alert out,
conduct random passenger searches.

823
00:58:37,542 --> 00:58:40,292
Kopek works the Northwind terminal.
Let's start there.

824
00:58:40,375 --> 00:58:42,083
I'll get the ball rolling with airport PD.

825
00:58:42,167 --> 00:58:45,542
They could use a head start given the
shitstorm we're about to drop on them.

826
00:58:45,625 --> 00:58:48,542
You drive.
Texting and driving is how I kill people.

827
00:58:49,417 --> 00:58:52,875
You're ordering a random sweep
of Terminal 7, middle of Christmas Eve,

828
00:58:52,958 --> 00:58:56,458
the busiest travel day of the year,
and you're not gonna tell me why?

829
00:58:57,875 --> 00:59:00,875
No, it's great.
People love missing their flights.

830
00:59:00,958 --> 00:59:03,208
They come to the airport for the sushi.

831
00:59:06,417 --> 00:59:10,083
<i>Attention. To ensure</i>
<i>the safety of those traveling today,</i>

832
00:59:10,167 --> 00:59:12,750
<i>the TSA will be performing
random bag checks.</i>

833
00:59:12,833 --> 00:59:15,500
<i>If you are selected,
please accompany the officer.</i>

834
00:59:15,583 --> 00:59:18,250
<i>Thank you for your cooperation,
and happy holidays.</i>

835
00:59:18,333 --> 00:59:21,125
<i>- </i><i>What's happening?</i>
- How should I know?

836
00:59:21,208 --> 00:59:24,583
We got a situation. I'm gonna
need you to shut down all the lines.

837
00:59:24,667 --> 00:59:26,333
- All the lines?
- Yes. All of them.

838
00:59:31,792 --> 00:59:35,500
All right, listen up.
All lines are officially on hold.

839
00:59:35,583 --> 00:59:37,542
<i>Everyone meet in the office. Right now.</i>

840
00:59:45,792 --> 00:59:46,958
Just one second.

841
00:59:53,875 --> 00:59:57,083
Except you, Samir.
You deal with that. Good luck.

842
01:00:05,167 --> 01:00:07,708
Y'all heard the call.
We're doing random sweeps.

843
01:00:07,792 --> 01:00:10,000
- How many?
- I got a list of 50 passengers.

844
01:00:10,083 --> 01:00:11,375
- Fifty?
- Yeah.

845
01:00:11,458 --> 01:00:14,375
When we're done,
I'll have it sent to your MDTs, okay?

846
01:00:15,250 --> 01:00:20,000
Work with the LEOs, find these people,
and bring them in for inspection, okay?

847
01:00:20,083 --> 01:00:21,750
Gonna really slow things down.

848
01:00:21,833 --> 01:00:23,634
- No shit.
- I didn't see an alert.

849
01:00:23,708 --> 01:00:27,208
Didn't get an official alert.
I just got a heads-up from the LAPD.

850
01:00:27,292 --> 01:00:29,875
So let's go over some protocols.

851
01:00:29,958 --> 01:00:33,792
Lance, you and Samir are gonna be working
crowd control. Keep the lanes open.

852
01:00:34,375 --> 01:00:37,083
The rest of us, we divide and conquer.

853
01:00:37,167 --> 01:00:41,292
Okay, Ron? Need you to open up
the back rooms for inspection.

854
01:00:42,292 --> 01:00:44,042
<i>Do you have eyes on him?</i>

855
01:00:44,667 --> 01:00:47,083
No. The whole room is a blind spot.

856
01:00:47,917 --> 01:00:50,500
Some of these passengers
won't be happy.

857
01:00:50,583 --> 01:00:52,500
They give you shit,
you send them to me.

858
01:00:52,583 --> 01:00:54,292
- Yep.
- This shit sounds serious.

859
01:00:54,375 --> 01:00:58,208
- Is it weird I'm excited?
- Guys, don't get excited.

860
01:00:58,292 --> 01:00:59,708
Just our buddies at the LAPD

861
01:00:59,792 --> 01:01:01,750
- justifying their budget.
- This sucks.

862
01:01:01,833 --> 01:01:03,542
Look, I know it sucks.

863
01:01:03,625 --> 01:01:06,250
We can either waste our time
saying how much it sucks

864
01:01:06,333 --> 01:01:08,917
or we get out and do our job
and find these people.

865
01:01:09,000 --> 01:01:10,708
- So, let's go. Come on.
- All right.

866
01:01:12,292 --> 01:01:13,667
Hey, uh, Ethan.

867
01:01:15,083 --> 01:01:18,292
I know it's been
a particularly stressful day for you,

868
01:01:18,375 --> 01:01:19,833
what with Jason and Lionel,

869
01:01:19,917 --> 01:01:21,542
so appreciate you digging in.

870
01:01:23,708 --> 01:01:25,625
I can see you want to be here.

871
01:01:37,375 --> 01:01:39,875
I know what you did.

872
01:01:41,125 --> 01:01:42,958
And I know why you did it.

873
01:01:43,792 --> 01:01:46,333
Just didn't think
you'd be that kind of guy, bro.

874
01:01:48,000 --> 01:01:49,625
Good luck with your promotion.

875
01:01:51,125 --> 01:01:52,625
Jason, I can fix this.

876
01:01:54,792 --> 01:01:56,417
Don't ever talk to me again.

877
01:02:03,625 --> 01:02:04,708
<i>You alone?</i>

878
01:02:05,125 --> 01:02:06,292
Yeah.

879
01:02:06,375 --> 01:02:07,875
<i>Good, get back to work.</i>

880
01:02:09,000 --> 01:02:12,500
<i>Attention. To ensure</i>
<i>the safety of those traveling today,</i>

881
01:02:12,583 --> 01:02:15,500
<i>the TSA will be performing
random bag checks.</i>

882
01:02:15,583 --> 01:02:18,792
<i>The following passengers
are to report to a TSA officer.</i>

883
01:02:18,875 --> 01:02:22,167
<i>Carrie Pierce. Cameron Figgs.
Mateo Flores. Alison Mallory.</i>

884
01:02:22,250 --> 01:02:24,875
<i>Ethan, what did you do?</i>

885
01:02:25,667 --> 01:02:27,917
Nothing, I didn't move.

886
01:02:28,000 --> 01:02:30,375
Why'd they pull my guy?

887
01:02:30,458 --> 01:02:32,042
It's a lottery system.

888
01:02:35,333 --> 01:02:36,417
Right in here.

889
01:02:39,542 --> 01:02:42,208
You're lying. I don't know
how you did this, but this is you.

890
01:02:46,458 --> 01:02:49,375
Sit right back down.
You leave that post, you're in breach.

891
01:02:50,042 --> 01:02:51,750
There's nothing I can do.

892
01:02:51,833 --> 01:02:52,958
Hey.

893
01:02:53,042 --> 01:02:54,250
This is over.

894
01:02:54,333 --> 01:02:55,542
<i>Hey, Ethan...</i>

895
01:03:06,875 --> 01:03:08,792
He's on his way down. Change his mind.

896
01:03:09,375 --> 01:03:10,375
Copy that.

897
01:03:14,833 --> 01:03:16,167
Let's go for a ride.

898
01:03:37,875 --> 01:03:38,875
Hey!

899
01:03:52,667 --> 01:03:53,667
Hey!

900
01:03:54,667 --> 01:03:55,708
We gotta go.

901
01:03:55,792 --> 01:03:56,958
What? Why?

902
01:04:06,500 --> 01:04:08,667
- Rochelle texted me.
- No…

903
01:04:08,750 --> 01:04:11,430
- She said you got Jason fired.
- I can explain but we have to move.

904
01:04:11,458 --> 01:04:12,833
- So it's true?
- I had to!

905
01:04:13,833 --> 01:04:14,833
I don't understand.

906
01:04:17,708 --> 01:04:19,208
To get a promotion?

907
01:04:19,292 --> 01:04:20,917
Why would you do that?

908
01:04:26,833 --> 01:04:29,167
<i>You speak one word,</i>
<i>and she dies.</i>

909
01:04:29,250 --> 01:04:31,292
<i>You have three seconds to back away</i>

910
01:04:31,375 --> 01:04:33,792
<i>or a 30-caliber round
will travel 3,000 feet per second</i>

911
01:04:33,875 --> 01:04:36,083
<i>and paint the wall with her brain. Three…</i>

912
01:04:36,167 --> 01:04:38,167
Ethan, I need you to talk to me.

913
01:04:38,250 --> 01:04:39,458
<i>Two…</i>

914
01:04:40,667 --> 01:04:42,083
This isn't you.

915
01:04:44,167 --> 01:04:45,583
<i>Not one word.</i>

916
01:04:46,542 --> 01:04:48,000
So you're just walking away?

917
01:05:00,667 --> 01:05:03,042
<i>Departure gate for Flight 3678…</i>

918
01:05:06,875 --> 01:05:09,500
I was patient with you
because I thought I liked you.

919
01:05:11,292 --> 01:05:12,667
Come here.

920
01:05:16,292 --> 01:05:19,292
People tell you who they are
long before they open up their mouths.

921
01:05:19,375 --> 01:05:22,958
You know what you told me?
That you're pathetic and you're asleep.

922
01:05:23,042 --> 01:05:25,042
You're someone that's
so afraid to make a mistake,

923
01:05:25,125 --> 01:05:27,208
you're willing to let
the whole world pass you by.

924
01:05:27,292 --> 01:05:29,458
- That's how I knew you were my guy.
- I lied.

925
01:05:30,792 --> 01:05:32,208
What's that?

926
01:05:32,292 --> 01:05:36,500
I lied on the polygraph.
That's why I didn't get into the academy.

927
01:05:36,583 --> 01:05:39,417
- Yeah? What'd you lie about?
- Well, I told him that…

928
01:05:39,500 --> 01:05:40,500
Speak up.

929
01:05:43,958 --> 01:05:44,958
Come here.

930
01:05:45,042 --> 01:05:47,542
You think you can take control? Huh?

931
01:05:47,625 --> 01:05:51,125
You haven't been in control since you were
on that shitty track team in high school.

932
01:05:51,208 --> 01:05:53,750
So proud of the way
you can run fast in circles?

933
01:05:54,792 --> 01:05:57,208
High school was as good
as your life would get,

934
01:05:57,292 --> 01:05:59,125
so this will be a mercy kill.

935
01:06:01,208 --> 01:06:04,833
Okay, okay, all right, all right.
Take it easy. Take it easy.

936
01:06:04,917 --> 01:06:08,000
That's great.
Well, at least this is interesting.

937
01:06:09,250 --> 01:06:10,250
What now?

938
01:06:10,333 --> 01:06:12,875
First, you're gonna call your sniper

939
01:06:12,958 --> 01:06:17,000
and when I confirm Nora's okay,
then I am walking you out to the police.

940
01:06:17,083 --> 01:06:20,250
What if I do none of that
'cause the odds of you pulling that...

941
01:06:21,500 --> 01:06:22,708
Let's do it your way.

942
01:06:24,500 --> 01:06:26,375
- Okay. Slowly.
- Yep.

943
01:06:27,875 --> 01:06:29,458
Then we're gonna do the phone.

944
01:06:31,542 --> 01:06:34,167
All right? Let's take care of it.

945
01:06:36,167 --> 01:06:37,167
Here we go.

946
01:06:45,542 --> 01:06:46,542
What's the code?

947
01:06:48,042 --> 01:06:49,042
The code?

948
01:06:50,625 --> 01:06:53,500
You got ten minutes
before everybody in this airport dies.

949
01:06:54,000 --> 01:06:56,417
- Shut it down.
- Payload will spread through all the ducts

950
01:06:56,500 --> 01:06:58,792
in all the terminals in this airport
with 100% lethality...

951
01:06:58,875 --> 01:07:00,208
I said shut it down!

952
01:07:00,292 --> 01:07:03,375
I can't from here, buddy, okay?

953
01:07:03,458 --> 01:07:06,208
Even if I wanted to, and I do want to
since I'm in this building.

954
01:07:06,292 --> 01:07:07,917
I'll have to put my hands on it.

955
01:07:08,000 --> 01:07:11,958
Okay, come on, you're not gonna
shoot me, Ethan. Think about it.

956
01:07:12,042 --> 01:07:15,125
What happens after that?
I can disarm it in a minute-thirty,

957
01:07:15,208 --> 01:07:16,792
I know what I'm doing. Do you?

958
01:07:16,875 --> 01:07:20,167
Or maybe your Explosives Disposal Unit
can get there in time? I doubt it.

959
01:07:20,250 --> 01:07:23,750
Would you rather kill 250 people
on a plane or 5,000 in an airport?

960
01:07:23,833 --> 01:07:25,875
On Christmas Eve
it's probably closer to 10,000.

961
01:07:25,958 --> 01:07:28,750
That's the thing with numbers.
They all get larger.

962
01:07:28,833 --> 01:07:30,208
Okay, go.

963
01:07:30,292 --> 01:07:31,625
No, you go. Go to the case

964
01:07:31,708 --> 01:07:34,708
and I'll walk you through
how to turn off that timer, okay?

965
01:07:34,792 --> 01:07:37,167
But don't talk to anybody.
Open up that mouth, I close mine.

966
01:07:37,250 --> 01:07:40,000
- Why are you making me do it?
- 'Cause you're not in control, Ethan,

967
01:07:40,083 --> 01:07:42,708
and you never will be.
Clock's ticking. So, go.

968
01:07:42,792 --> 01:07:44,333
Take the gun. Maybe run.

969
01:07:55,708 --> 01:07:57,292
And the other side, same thing?

970
01:07:57,875 --> 01:08:01,292
No, sorry. That's the…
I made a mistake on the first side.

971
01:08:03,167 --> 01:08:04,375
Three.

972
01:08:09,833 --> 01:08:11,042
<i>Is he alone?</i>

973
01:08:12,292 --> 01:08:15,083
- Doesn't seem to be working.
- I think my boss is in there with him.

974
01:08:15,167 --> 01:08:17,125
That's fine.
Walk in and shoot the boss.

975
01:08:18,625 --> 01:08:19,917
- What?
<i>- Nothing fancy.</i>

976
01:08:20,000 --> 01:08:22,250
One in the head, two max.
It's a plastic gun.

977
01:08:22,333 --> 01:08:25,250
Each shot generates heat.
If it melts, it'll explode in your hands.

978
01:08:25,333 --> 01:08:27,250
No, I can't do that.

979
01:08:27,333 --> 01:08:29,750
Really? You seemed ready
to kill me a minute ago.

980
01:08:29,833 --> 01:08:32,268
- I can knock him out.
<i>- No. We don't have time to experiment.</i>

981
01:08:32,292 --> 01:08:35,458
They're gonna die along with everyone else
in this airport if the bomb explodes.

982
01:08:35,542 --> 01:08:36,542
You make the choice.

983
01:08:36,625 --> 01:08:38,958
And look, Nora finally stopped crying.

984
01:08:46,875 --> 01:08:48,667
- Back away.
- What are you doing?

985
01:08:48,750 --> 01:08:49,625
<i>Do it. Shoot him.</i>

986
01:08:49,708 --> 01:08:53,000
- I said back away from the case, please.
- All right. Backing away.

987
01:08:53,083 --> 01:08:55,792
Don't know what this is about,
but I know you don't want to do this.

988
01:08:55,875 --> 01:08:57,958
<i>If you don't do this,
a lot of people are gonna die.</i>

989
01:08:58,042 --> 01:08:59,333
I have to.

990
01:08:59,417 --> 01:09:00,500
About to be a father.

991
01:09:01,125 --> 01:09:04,458
Do you want your kid
growing up with this in his life?

992
01:09:08,292 --> 01:09:09,625
Put the gun down and we can talk.

993
01:09:09,708 --> 01:09:12,000
He's done enough talking.
You're wasting time.

994
01:09:12,083 --> 01:09:13,917
Shoot him now or everyone dies.

995
01:09:14,000 --> 01:09:16,000
Please, don't make me do this.

996
01:09:16,083 --> 01:09:18,417
<i>- Shoot him.</i>
- Who are you talking to?

997
01:09:19,042 --> 01:09:20,417
God damn it, do it now!

998
01:09:37,125 --> 01:09:40,875
Okay, and you're sure?
Okay. All right. Thanks, Marty.

999
01:09:40,958 --> 01:09:43,458
It's my partner.
He just pulled the FAA manifest.

1000
01:09:43,542 --> 01:09:45,917
There's no high-value targets
leaving LAX today.

1001
01:09:46,000 --> 01:09:47,583
That's fine.

1002
01:09:47,667 --> 01:09:50,750
We'll just talk to the Kopek guy.
He knows something.

1003
01:09:50,833 --> 01:09:52,917
Oh, God.

1004
01:09:57,542 --> 01:09:58,875
I need a first aid kit.

1005
01:09:58,958 --> 01:10:01,250
<i>No. Sounds like
your boss is past an ice pack.</i>

1006
01:10:01,333 --> 01:10:03,458
Just get to the package
or everyone dies with him.

1007
01:10:03,542 --> 01:10:05,333
I didn't have a choice.

1008
01:10:11,750 --> 01:10:13,875
No, no, no! Please don't kill Jesse!

1009
01:10:16,458 --> 01:10:18,083
I don't know who that is.

1010
01:10:18,167 --> 01:10:21,750
My husband. He took him from my house
and he gave me that case.

1011
01:10:25,000 --> 01:10:26,417
You're not with them?

1012
01:10:27,917 --> 01:10:28,917
I'm like you.

1013
01:10:31,125 --> 01:10:32,167
Give me the codes.

1014
01:10:32,250 --> 01:10:36,375
Left 109, right 083.

1015
01:10:43,958 --> 01:10:45,625
- Oh, God.
- What is that?

1016
01:10:45,708 --> 01:10:47,708
Be quiet. Lock the door.

1017
01:10:52,958 --> 01:10:54,167
Okay, what do I do?

1018
01:10:54,250 --> 01:10:56,375
<i>Do you see the two switches
on either side?</i>

1019
01:10:56,458 --> 01:11:00,208
<i>I want you to unlock those and then
lift it out of the case by the frame.</i>

1020
01:11:08,000 --> 01:11:09,042
Okay, done.

1021
01:11:09,125 --> 01:11:11,583
<i>There are two holes next to the timer.</i>

1022
01:11:11,667 --> 01:11:15,042
<i>Use them to turn
the circular plate clockwise,</i>

1023
01:11:15,125 --> 01:11:16,333
<i>then pull up.</i>

1024
01:11:19,042 --> 01:11:21,583
<i>Okay, now, disconnect the remote relay.</i>

1025
01:11:21,667 --> 01:11:24,042
The button under the circular plate,

1026
01:11:24,125 --> 01:11:27,167
<i>press it once to put it in manual mode.</i>

1027
01:11:30,875 --> 01:11:31,917
Good, good.

1028
01:11:32,000 --> 01:11:34,125
<i>Breathe if you haven't.</i>

1029
01:11:35,000 --> 01:11:39,500
<i>And then pull up on the handles
on the side of the cage slowly.</i>

1030
01:11:48,958 --> 01:11:51,042
There are two clusters.

1031
01:11:51,125 --> 01:11:52,583
<i>Grab the one on the right.</i>

1032
01:11:52,667 --> 01:11:53,750
<i>Pull it up slowly.</i>

1033
01:11:53,833 --> 01:11:56,833
<i>Once it's out,
you'll be able to see the reset button.</i>

1034
01:12:03,125 --> 01:12:04,583
Hey! Why is this door locked?

1035
01:12:08,792 --> 01:12:09,875
Just a minute.

1036
01:12:10,375 --> 01:12:12,500
Kopek? Why are you in there?

1037
01:12:13,208 --> 01:12:15,625
<i>There's a button that should be visible
between the brackets.</i>

1038
01:12:15,708 --> 01:12:17,250
<i>That'll reset the device.</i>

1039
01:12:20,583 --> 01:12:22,875
- I can't reach it.
- Let me in.

1040
01:12:26,750 --> 01:12:28,167
What are you doing?

1041
01:12:28,250 --> 01:12:30,708
- Put it down.
- I won't let Jesse die!

1042
01:12:30,792 --> 01:12:31,875
Open the door.

1043
01:12:33,208 --> 01:12:34,875
Look at me. Look at me!

1044
01:12:35,917 --> 01:12:37,125
I can do it.

1045
01:12:38,000 --> 01:12:39,167
Please. Trust me.

1046
01:12:39,250 --> 01:12:41,083
- Kopek!
<i>- </i><i>Thirty seconds.</i>

1047
01:13:00,708 --> 01:13:02,583
Kopek, open this door.

1048
01:13:10,500 --> 01:13:13,417
I'm not playing around.
Open the goddamn door right now.

1049
01:13:15,042 --> 01:13:16,458
- Yeah.
<i>- </i><i>You were right.</i>

1050
01:13:16,542 --> 01:13:18,583
My three favorite words. What about?

1051
01:13:18,667 --> 01:13:20,250
Officer Williams.

1052
01:13:20,333 --> 01:13:23,917
The ME found a scratch on the back
of his hand with traces of aconite.

1053
01:13:24,000 --> 01:13:26,542
A cardiotoxin
that causes ventricular arrhythmia.

1054
01:13:26,625 --> 01:13:27,917
Heart attack was induced.

1055
01:13:28,000 --> 01:13:30,250
Homeland's in play now too, by the way.

1056
01:13:30,333 --> 01:13:33,667
They finally decided to check
the FAA passenger manifest

1057
01:13:33,750 --> 01:13:36,458
to see if any high-value targets
were flying through Los Angeles.

1058
01:13:36,542 --> 01:13:38,458
- Uh-huh.
<i>- How about four of them?</i>

1059
01:13:40,292 --> 01:13:43,125
The hell is wrong with you,
leaving me outside like that?

1060
01:13:45,542 --> 01:13:48,375
I was just… finishing up a bag check.

1061
01:13:49,583 --> 01:13:50,958
The room's all yours.

1062
01:13:53,542 --> 01:13:55,542
We have four Marines coming from Arifjan

1063
01:13:55,625 --> 01:13:58,167
to testify before Congress
on that Aleppo incident.

1064
01:13:58,250 --> 01:14:00,792
- Did we get their flight info?
<i>- No. It's redacted.</i>

1065
01:14:00,875 --> 01:14:03,167
<i>But Homeland is sending
someone over with the raw data.</i>

1066
01:14:03,250 --> 01:14:05,667
Okay. Give me his name. I'll bring him.

1067
01:14:06,167 --> 01:14:08,583
<i>Agent John Alcott.</i>

1068
01:14:11,708 --> 01:14:12,708
Okay.

1069
01:14:13,708 --> 01:14:15,458
That's great. Do me a favor.

1070
01:14:15,542 --> 01:14:19,958
Brief Conley. Tell him I'm en route to LAX
with Agent John Alcott right now.

1071
01:14:20,042 --> 01:14:22,375
But that doesn't make any sense.
What are you...

1072
01:14:22,458 --> 01:14:23,875
Elena?

1073
01:14:25,833 --> 01:14:28,833
You carried out a search
without a lead or a LEO present?

1074
01:14:28,917 --> 01:14:30,917
Sarkowski got called away
to ticketing.

1075
01:14:31,000 --> 01:14:33,250
Just trying to, you know,
speed things along.

1076
01:14:37,833 --> 01:14:39,458
Something's going on with you.

1077
01:14:41,208 --> 01:14:43,250
And I'm gonna figure out what it is.

1078
01:14:52,583 --> 01:14:53,583
I'm Ethan.

1079
01:14:54,875 --> 01:14:56,292
- Mateo.
<i>- </i><i>No, no.</i>

1080
01:14:56,375 --> 01:14:59,458
Get acquainted later. You need to
dispose of that body and get moving.

1081
01:14:59,542 --> 01:15:00,958
Boarding time is in a half an hour.

1082
01:15:01,042 --> 01:15:03,000
- Everything all good?
- Yeah.

1083
01:15:04,208 --> 01:15:07,042
You know, the world
trying to make you feel like shit

1084
01:15:07,125 --> 01:15:10,417
because you go a whole five minutes
without checking your email

1085
01:15:10,500 --> 01:15:12,625
to enjoy a conversation.

1086
01:15:15,625 --> 01:15:17,375
- Who are you?
- Whoa.

1087
01:15:18,167 --> 01:15:20,583
Whoa, whoa.
John Alcott, okay? Homeland Security.

1088
01:15:20,667 --> 01:15:22,833
- I'm the guy who just backed your play.
- Mmm-mmm.

1089
01:15:22,917 --> 01:15:24,500
I offered to drive.

1090
01:15:24,583 --> 01:15:27,583
Agent John Alcott is on his way
to the station right now.

1091
01:15:31,292 --> 01:15:33,083
You intercepted my call to DHS.

1092
01:15:33,792 --> 01:15:36,708
Yeah, we've had a network
around your station for the last 72 hours.

1093
01:15:36,792 --> 01:15:40,000
Who's "we"?
And what do you want with the Novichok?

1094
01:15:44,542 --> 01:15:45,792
So what are you gonna do?

1095
01:15:45,875 --> 01:15:48,500
You're gonna shoot me
doing 70 down the highway?

1096
01:17:04,333 --> 01:17:07,542
We'll take him to sorting.
It's automated, no one will be there.

1097
01:17:08,125 --> 01:17:09,417
How'd you get involved?

1098
01:17:10,000 --> 01:17:11,333
I asked for a raise.

1099
01:17:19,292 --> 01:17:20,958
- Herschel… No.
<i>- Are you all right?</i>

1100
01:17:21,042 --> 01:17:24,250
No, not all right. Ping my phone.

1101
01:17:24,333 --> 01:17:25,958
Send somebody to ID the body.

1102
01:17:26,042 --> 01:17:27,042
<i>- A body?</i>
- Yeah.

1103
01:17:27,583 --> 01:17:30,167
Alcott… wasn't Alcott.

1104
01:17:30,250 --> 01:17:33,917
<i>What the hell does that mean?
Elena? Elena?</i>

1105
01:17:34,000 --> 01:17:35,208
Police.

1106
01:17:35,958 --> 01:17:37,667
- Oh, my God!
- Police.

1107
01:17:37,750 --> 01:17:40,167
- Are you okay? Okay.
- I'm police, I need the car.

1108
01:17:40,250 --> 01:17:42,083
I'm not playing, I need the car.

1109
01:17:44,708 --> 01:17:47,917
My man Ethan.
They spring you for Christmas?

1110
01:17:48,000 --> 01:17:51,083
No, not yet.
I gotta run this to sorting first.

1111
01:17:51,167 --> 01:17:52,917
I can take it. Let's get you home.

1112
01:17:53,000 --> 01:17:54,500
No, it's okay. I got it.

1113
01:17:54,583 --> 01:17:56,417
It's no problem. I could take this...

1114
01:17:56,500 --> 01:17:57,708
I said I got it.

1115
01:18:00,125 --> 01:18:01,125
Merry Christmas.

1116
01:18:03,042 --> 01:18:05,167
<i> Mateo, can you, um…</i>

1117
01:18:05,250 --> 01:18:06,875
<i>Sorry, I'm eating.</i>

1118
01:18:06,958 --> 01:18:10,375
Mateo, I'm speaking just to you now.
Cough if you understand.

1119
01:18:11,750 --> 01:18:15,125
Okay. I want you to listen,
but do not speak. Hold on.

1120
01:18:16,958 --> 01:18:18,375
<i>Okay, put him through.</i>

1121
01:18:20,500 --> 01:18:21,917
Mateo, it's me.

1122
01:18:22,000 --> 01:18:25,542
<i>I'm okay.
They say you've done really well,</i>

1123
01:18:25,625 --> 01:18:27,167
<i>and that you're almost done.</i>

1124
01:18:29,375 --> 01:18:31,958
<i>They say there's one more thing
that you have to do.</i>

1125
01:20:10,833 --> 01:20:15,292
Mateo! Listen to me. If you keep firing...

1126
01:21:31,042 --> 01:21:33,625
I'm… sorry…

1127
01:22:02,292 --> 01:22:04,583
We got here two hours early
like you told us to.

1128
01:22:04,667 --> 01:22:07,417
- TSA is completely disorganized.
- I know, sir.

1129
01:22:08,458 --> 01:22:09,542
Sir.

1130
01:22:10,917 --> 01:22:12,250
This is a restricted area.

1131
01:22:27,208 --> 01:22:29,458
Hey, miss. Miss!

1132
01:22:30,125 --> 01:22:32,833
Hey, you can't leave your car here. Hey!

1133
01:22:32,917 --> 01:22:36,000
…right here, we'll pull up
the outgoing flights to Jackson.

1134
01:22:39,792 --> 01:22:43,750
<i>Hey, it's Nora. Please leave</i>
<i>me a message and I'll get back to you…</i>

1135
01:22:46,042 --> 01:22:48,250
This new $anto$
is streaming on SoundCloud.

1136
01:22:48,333 --> 01:22:50,542
Forget Lil Nas X, forget Cardi B, baby.

1137
01:22:50,625 --> 01:22:53,500
It's the hottest thing on SoundCloud
right now, I promise.

1138
01:23:16,833 --> 01:23:18,042
LAPD!

1139
01:23:37,667 --> 01:23:39,167
Where's the security director?

1140
01:23:39,250 --> 01:23:42,083
Sarkowski? I think he's in ticketing.
Can I help you?

1141
01:23:42,167 --> 01:23:45,833
I need a line to LAX Security Tower
and I need to talk to Ethan Kopek.

1142
01:23:46,917 --> 01:23:50,333
Checkpoint Blue to STSO.
Do you have eyes on Kopek?

1143
01:23:52,000 --> 01:23:53,708
Checkpoint Blue to STSO.

1144
01:23:54,625 --> 01:23:56,000
Sarkowski, do you copy?

1145
01:23:56,083 --> 01:23:59,167
<i>Yeah, you looking for E?</i>
<i>He's on the way to sorting.</i>

1146
01:23:59,250 --> 01:24:01,917
What is he doing down there?
The guy's been acting wiggly all day.

1147
01:24:02,000 --> 01:24:03,500
Shut this checkpoint down now

1148
01:24:03,583 --> 01:24:05,792
and put Tower on notice
for all Northwind flights.

1149
01:24:05,875 --> 01:24:07,042
You take me down there?

1150
01:24:07,125 --> 01:24:09,333
- Yeah, follow me.
- What's going on?

1151
01:24:18,083 --> 01:24:20,667
Ethan? Ethan!

1152
01:24:21,625 --> 01:24:23,125
Give me that case!

1153
01:24:32,167 --> 01:24:33,875
Can you hear me? Looks like I nicked you.

1154
01:24:33,958 --> 01:24:36,708
<i>Hope you're all right. Give me
the goddamn case or Nora dies.</i>

1155
01:24:36,792 --> 01:24:38,792
<i>I don't wanna play hide-and-seek.</i>

1156
01:24:42,667 --> 01:24:45,667
<i>Ethan, I don't want any more nonsense.
Roll the case out.</i>

1157
01:25:03,375 --> 01:25:07,625
All right. I'm done. Play it your way.
Listen up. Kill the girl.

1158
01:25:07,708 --> 01:25:08,708
Copy that.

1159
01:26:15,083 --> 01:26:16,500
Merry Christmas.

1160
01:26:26,625 --> 01:26:30,250
"Sniper in short-term. White van.
Ready Teddy. Get Nora to police."

1161
01:26:30,333 --> 01:26:33,667
"Terrorists Northwind 1850." This is real?

1162
01:26:33,750 --> 01:26:36,208
Hell if I know.
He's been acting all suss all day.

1163
01:26:36,292 --> 01:26:37,333
Talking to himself.

1164
01:26:37,417 --> 01:26:38,833
What's a "Ready Teddy"?

1165
01:26:47,167 --> 01:26:48,167
Eddie?

1166
01:26:50,458 --> 01:26:51,458
Move.

1167
01:26:57,333 --> 01:26:59,542
Head to the cops downstairs.

1168
01:26:59,625 --> 01:27:00,833
I got this.

1169
01:27:02,500 --> 01:27:04,875
Hey, man. What's up?
I got the deal for you.

1170
01:27:04,958 --> 01:27:07,125
Upgrade to business class select
right now...

1171
01:27:21,250 --> 01:27:22,917
What the hell is that doing here?

1172
01:27:23,000 --> 01:27:25,208
- What's the problem?
- That shouldn't be here.

1173
01:27:30,917 --> 01:27:33,458
Confirm with LAX Tower,
we have an active threat.

1174
01:27:33,542 --> 01:27:36,125
Pull all Northwind flights
and shut down Terminal 7.

1175
01:27:36,750 --> 01:27:40,625
This is Dunn. I need you to shut down
Terminal 7. We have an active threat.

1176
01:27:41,917 --> 01:27:45,750
Sir? TSA and LAPD confirmed
a live threat in Terminal 7.

1177
01:27:45,833 --> 01:27:47,958
Shut down 7 and all of Northwind.

1178
01:27:48,042 --> 01:27:51,250
But I'm not shutting down LAX
and grounding 300 planes on Christmas Eve

1179
01:27:51,333 --> 01:27:53,250
without a direct call from Homeland.

1180
01:27:59,417 --> 01:28:02,875
Baggage recovered,
but we lost our courier. Bring me a kit.

1181
01:28:25,542 --> 01:28:27,625
Hey! Help!

1182
01:29:03,042 --> 01:29:04,833
Don't move!

1183
01:29:04,917 --> 01:29:07,000
LAPD! Hands! Let's go!

1184
01:29:07,083 --> 01:29:08,125
Are you Kopek?

1185
01:29:08,208 --> 01:29:09,458
No, wait… No. Wait!

1186
01:29:19,292 --> 01:29:23,000
I know this looks bad, but you have to
let me go, I have to get to my girlfriend.

1187
01:29:23,083 --> 01:29:24,250
No. You are coming with me

1188
01:29:24,333 --> 01:29:27,000
and you're gonna tell me all about
the nerve gas. Now, where is it?

1189
01:29:27,083 --> 01:29:29,042
He still has it. Listen. Listen!

1190
01:29:29,125 --> 01:29:32,458
He's trying to take out Northwind 1850.
All passengers.

1191
01:29:32,542 --> 01:29:34,601
- I don't know if there's a target...
- You been shot?

1192
01:29:34,625 --> 01:29:37,042
I've been trying to stop them.
They threatened my girlfriend.

1193
01:29:37,125 --> 01:29:39,458
- There's someone after her.
- You're coming with me.

1194
01:29:42,000 --> 01:29:44,333
I'm sorry. He's getting on Northwind 1850.

1195
01:29:44,417 --> 01:29:48,667
White male. American. Fifties. Black hat,
black case with a red ribbon on it.

1196
01:29:48,750 --> 01:29:51,583
He's got ground support
and he's tapped into the cameras.

1197
01:29:51,667 --> 01:29:53,500
These guys are professionals!

1198
01:30:15,917 --> 01:30:17,333
Maybe see who could explain?

1199
01:30:17,417 --> 01:30:18,667
- I'm sorry.
- Where's Nora?

1200
01:30:18,750 --> 01:30:20,250
I saw her go downstairs.

1201
01:30:23,083 --> 01:30:24,292
Get out of the way!

1202
01:30:46,333 --> 01:30:47,333
Help!

1203
01:30:47,417 --> 01:30:48,833
Help!

1204
01:31:12,917 --> 01:31:13,833
- You okay?
- Yeah.

1205
01:31:13,917 --> 01:31:14,917
They hurt you?

1206
01:31:29,375 --> 01:31:30,625
You're Jesse?

1207
01:31:32,458 --> 01:31:35,333
My husband, Mateo Flores, is he…

1208
01:31:42,417 --> 01:31:44,375
He did everything he could to save you.

1209
01:31:45,167 --> 01:31:46,917
They said everything would be fine.

1210
01:31:47,417 --> 01:31:50,500
If he did what they wanted, they'd let him
fly back from DC tomorrow.

1211
01:31:50,583 --> 01:31:51,583
DC?

1212
01:31:52,917 --> 01:31:55,250
He's not supposed to be
on the New York flight?

1213
01:31:55,333 --> 01:31:57,167
They gave him two tickets.

1214
01:32:02,667 --> 01:32:06,250
<i>Turner doesn't have the votes</i>
<i>because DTD is unconscionable.</i>

1215
01:32:06,333 --> 01:32:08,750
<i>You cannot underride
record military spending</i>

1216
01:32:08,833 --> 01:32:12,583
<i>while failing to account for the billions
that are handed out every year</i>

1217
01:32:12,667 --> 01:32:15,458
<i>to spectacularly profitable
private contractors.</i>

1218
01:32:15,542 --> 01:32:18,292
<i>To ensure global stability</i>
<i>and peace it is imperative…</i>

1219
01:32:18,375 --> 01:32:20,250
Look who's on TV.

1220
01:32:20,333 --> 01:32:22,208
Well,
she's everywhere these days.

1221
01:32:22,292 --> 01:32:24,458
<i>…to defend threatened democracies
protects our allies…</i>

1222
01:32:24,542 --> 01:32:25,375
Yeah.

1223
01:32:25,458 --> 01:32:28,542
<i>…and keeps conflict from our borders.
This strategy not only safeguards…</i>

1224
01:32:28,625 --> 01:32:30,250
Have a safe flight.

1225
01:32:30,333 --> 01:32:33,750
<i>…but it also serves as a deterrent
against potential aggressors.</i>

1226
01:32:33,833 --> 01:32:38,042
<i>By investing in the defense
of democracies, we create stronger…</i>

1227
01:32:40,500 --> 01:32:43,250
LAXPD is aware
and sending you every hand on deck.

1228
01:32:43,333 --> 01:32:47,042
Everything coming into Terminal 7
is rerouted to Burbank or Long Beach.

1229
01:32:47,125 --> 01:32:49,958
But I have 60,000 passengers
in the rest of this airport.

1230
01:32:50,042 --> 01:32:51,542
<i>And I gotta keep them moving.</i>

1231
01:32:51,625 --> 01:32:54,583
Send me everything you got.
I'll let you know what we find.

1232
01:32:55,875 --> 01:32:56,708
Herschel?

1233
01:32:56,792 --> 01:32:59,292
Perfect timing. This just got super weird.

1234
01:32:59,375 --> 01:33:01,000
You can't surprise me today.

1235
01:33:01,083 --> 01:33:02,083
<i>I'll try.</i>

1236
01:33:02,167 --> 01:33:04,292
Fake Alcott is former Intelligence.

1237
01:33:04,375 --> 01:33:06,208
Any relationship with the Russians?

1238
01:33:06,292 --> 01:33:10,542
Not that I can find. He was discharged
under some heavily redacted circumstances,

1239
01:33:10,625 --> 01:33:13,333
then went freelance
for defense contractors.

1240
01:33:13,417 --> 01:33:16,250
Highest bidder types. They bid high.

1241
01:33:16,333 --> 01:33:20,125
Kopek said these guys are spread wide
and tapped in. Even painted a suspect.

1242
01:33:20,208 --> 01:33:21,833
Kopek? The guy who called us?

1243
01:33:21,917 --> 01:33:24,542
<i>- You trust him?</i>
- Keep looking for possible targets.

1244
01:33:24,625 --> 01:33:26,958
Start with Flight 1850,
and then widen the net.

1245
01:33:27,042 --> 01:33:29,250
Everybody with a flight today,
anybody with a profile.

1246
01:33:29,333 --> 01:33:30,375
Yeah, on it.

1247
01:33:30,458 --> 01:33:34,167
<i>Attention. All flights</i>
<i>departing from Terminal 7 are delayed.</i>

1248
01:33:34,250 --> 01:33:38,875
White male, fifties, black hat,
black case with a red ribbon.

1249
01:33:38,958 --> 01:33:41,333
Find him and do not let him board.

1250
01:33:43,125 --> 01:33:45,667
Oh, sweetie. Are you ready to fly?

1251
01:33:46,375 --> 01:33:48,833
Hello! He's so cute.

1252
01:33:49,917 --> 01:33:51,958
- How old is he?
- Eleven months old today.

1253
01:33:52,042 --> 01:33:54,625
- Have a safe flight, Congresswoman. Bye.
- Thank you.

1254
01:34:03,792 --> 01:34:06,458
I got an album coming out in two days.
You know what I'm saying?

1255
01:34:06,542 --> 01:34:09,833
It's on SoundCloud. Patreon.

1256
01:34:10,458 --> 01:34:12,042
We gotta find this bag.

1257
01:34:12,542 --> 01:34:13,625
I got this.

1258
01:34:17,417 --> 01:34:19,375
Nora Parisi, Airport Operations.

1259
01:34:28,750 --> 01:34:30,708
What's your seat number?

1260
01:34:36,208 --> 01:34:38,750
If the bag is scanned,
then I can find it anywhere.

1261
01:34:40,375 --> 01:34:41,375
Sorry.

1262
01:34:42,333 --> 01:34:45,792
Sir, I'm afraid that's too big to fit
as a carry-on. I can check it for you.

1263
01:34:45,875 --> 01:34:49,375
- No, I promise you I measured it myself.
- See, it's already been flagged.

1264
01:34:53,125 --> 01:34:55,542
I'll take it to cargo myself.
It'll be there when we land.

1265
01:34:55,625 --> 01:34:58,833
I promise. Would you like
to take anything out of it now?

1266
01:35:01,000 --> 01:35:02,000
No.

1267
01:35:03,750 --> 01:35:05,167
- Thank you.
- All right.

1268
01:35:05,250 --> 01:35:10,500
Ready? Five, five, two, six, eight,
four, four, zero, three, five.

1269
01:35:24,333 --> 01:35:27,167
I got it. It's on Trans Global 0610
to Washington, DC.

1270
01:35:27,250 --> 01:35:29,708
They boarded.
I'll call Tower and stop the flight.

1271
01:35:29,792 --> 01:35:33,542
No. Wait, wait. If we stop the flight,
he'll just trigger it on the ground.

1272
01:35:33,625 --> 01:35:35,000
It'll kill everyone anyway.

1273
01:35:35,667 --> 01:35:38,708
I diffused it once. I can do it again.

1274
01:35:41,667 --> 01:35:43,125
I know what to do.

1275
01:35:43,667 --> 01:35:46,125
There's an LAPD detective
trying to stop the bomb.

1276
01:35:46,208 --> 01:35:49,000
Find her, tell her
she has to let that plane take off.

1277
01:35:58,333 --> 01:35:59,417
- Hey.
<i>-  Hey.</i>

1278
01:35:59,500 --> 01:36:01,917
That Aleppo case, it was a dead end.

1279
01:36:02,000 --> 01:36:05,250
Marines say the confession scrapped
the need to testify. Anything?

1280
01:36:05,333 --> 01:36:08,292
Maybe. Found someone traveling
with a small security detail,

1281
01:36:08,375 --> 01:36:09,792
but in a different terminal.

1282
01:36:09,875 --> 01:36:12,792
Name is Grace Suarez.

1283
01:36:13,250 --> 01:36:15,000
Wait. Hang on. That's Grace Turner.

1284
01:36:15,083 --> 01:36:16,417
<i>The Congresswoman.</i>

1285
01:36:16,500 --> 01:36:18,500
Her office has her flying under
her maiden name.

1286
01:36:18,583 --> 01:36:19,875
<i>That's why she wasn't flagged.</i>

1287
01:36:19,958 --> 01:36:22,125
<i>Ladies and gentlemen, this is the captain.</i>

1288
01:36:22,208 --> 01:36:25,792
<i>Merry Christmas and welcome aboard
Trans Global Air Flight 0610</i>

1289
01:36:25,875 --> 01:36:28,208
<i>with nonstop service to Washington, DC.</i>

1290
01:36:28,292 --> 01:36:30,708
She has been the face of DTD,

1291
01:36:30,792 --> 01:36:34,125
a huge spend for threatened democracies
around the globe.

1292
01:36:34,208 --> 01:36:38,083
Weapons manufacturers are all over this
thing, but she doesn't have the votes.

1293
01:36:38,833 --> 01:36:40,542
Think the Russians want to take her out?

1294
01:36:40,625 --> 01:36:42,542
Kopek said these guys are American.

1295
01:36:42,625 --> 01:36:45,292
Fake Alcott, a hired gun
for defense contractors.

1296
01:36:46,208 --> 01:36:49,208
It's a set-up. Plane full of people,

1297
01:36:49,292 --> 01:36:53,208
Congresswoman, all killed
by Russian nerve toxin on Christmas Eve.

1298
01:36:53,292 --> 01:36:56,208
Everyone blames the Russians for killing
the one who stood up to them.

1299
01:36:56,292 --> 01:36:59,708
<i>Congress would rally around her bill,
open up a firehose of funding.</i>

1300
01:36:59,792 --> 01:37:01,833
Private contractors
get more than they ever dreamed.

1301
01:37:01,917 --> 01:37:05,292
All they had to do was kill one of their
own and everybody on board with her.

1302
01:37:05,375 --> 01:37:08,375
- What flight is she on?
<i>- Trans Global 610.</i>

1303
01:37:08,458 --> 01:37:10,583
Tower needs to ground that plane now.

1304
01:37:48,083 --> 01:37:49,750
Where's Trans Global 610 now?

1305
01:37:49,833 --> 01:37:53,167
Taxiing to the runway,
preparing for departure.

1306
01:37:53,250 --> 01:37:55,417
You need to stall it.
Keep it on the ground.

1307
01:37:55,500 --> 01:37:56,500
Is this your guy?

1308
01:37:56,583 --> 01:38:00,250
It's a delicate situation. We can't do
anything to spook anybody on board.

1309
01:38:00,333 --> 01:38:02,292
Tell them it's a mechanical issue,
a delay.

1310
01:38:02,375 --> 01:38:03,792
Why? What am I dealing with?

1311
01:38:03,875 --> 01:38:05,208
Are you with LAPD?

1312
01:38:05,833 --> 01:38:06,917
You can't ground 610.

1313
01:38:07,500 --> 01:38:08,625
And who are you?

1314
01:38:08,708 --> 01:38:10,625
Nora Parisi, Northwind Operations.

1315
01:38:10,708 --> 01:38:13,542
You just tried to arrest
my boyfriend Ethan Kopek.

1316
01:38:13,625 --> 01:38:15,042
You can't ground that plane.

1317
01:38:15,125 --> 01:38:17,125
<i>Detective, we have 610 on the line.</i>

1318
01:38:17,208 --> 01:38:18,833
Yeah. Tell them to hold on.

1319
01:38:18,917 --> 01:38:22,083
<i>Trans Global 610,</i>
<i>you are not yet cleared for takeoff.</i>

1320
01:38:22,167 --> 01:38:24,375
<i>Please stand by for further instructions.</i>

1321
01:38:24,458 --> 01:38:26,875
I know what's on it.
Tell your boyfriend to stay out of it.

1322
01:38:26,958 --> 01:38:29,125
We've got a trained killer
on board with a bomb.

1323
01:38:29,208 --> 01:38:31,500
And the moment he sees
anyone coming, he will set it off.

1324
01:38:31,583 --> 01:38:34,833
Ethan can disarm it without him knowing.
It's the only way.

1325
01:38:39,542 --> 01:38:42,208
So you expect me
to risk a plane full of people

1326
01:38:42,292 --> 01:38:46,125
because your boyfriend who decked me
says he can defuse a bomb mid-flight?

1327
01:38:46,208 --> 01:38:48,125
He did it before, he can do it again.

1328
01:38:49,250 --> 01:38:52,167
Detective, we have 610 holding.
What am I doing here?

1329
01:39:00,792 --> 01:39:02,208
It's the only way.

1330
01:39:05,042 --> 01:39:07,167
LA Tower,
what's the reason for the holdup?

1331
01:39:10,042 --> 01:39:12,875
<i>Trans Global 0610,</i>
<i>we have a Code 4 on the ground.</i>

1332
01:39:12,958 --> 01:39:14,625
<i>We're trying to assess with local PD.</i>

1333
01:39:15,208 --> 01:39:16,208
<i>Detective?</i>

1334
01:39:17,333 --> 01:39:18,333
Tower…

1335
01:39:20,000 --> 01:39:22,250
Allow 0610 to take off.

1336
01:39:22,333 --> 01:39:23,333
You sure?

1337
01:39:24,542 --> 01:39:25,958
You heard me.

1338
01:39:30,500 --> 01:39:32,833
Good news, folks.
We've received the all clear.

1339
01:39:32,917 --> 01:39:35,333
<i>Flight attendants,
prepare for takeoff, please.</i>

1340
01:42:03,500 --> 01:42:04,500
Ethan!

1341
01:42:06,167 --> 01:42:08,417
This stopped being funny
the last time I shot you.

1342
01:42:08,500 --> 01:42:11,708
Nice touch switching out the bags.
Put that down and step away from it.

1343
01:42:11,792 --> 01:42:14,167
I'm dead anyway
if I let you set this thing off.

1344
01:42:14,750 --> 01:42:16,250
Might as well shoot me again.

1345
01:42:17,000 --> 01:42:18,000
Okay.

1346
01:42:20,708 --> 01:42:22,375
Movement in cargo hold, checking.

1347
01:42:29,458 --> 01:42:31,458
It's over, pal.
It was over the minute I met you.

1348
01:42:31,542 --> 01:42:33,458
You don't know shit about me.

1349
01:42:33,542 --> 01:42:36,542
LA Tower, we have
two armed individuals aboard the aircraft.

1350
01:42:36,625 --> 01:42:37,833
We're declaring an emergency.

1351
01:42:39,375 --> 01:42:41,875
<i>Ladies and gentlemen,
this is the captain speaking.</i>

1352
01:42:41,958 --> 01:42:44,042
<i>For your safety, we are returning to LAX.</i>

1353
01:42:44,125 --> 01:42:46,417
<i>Flight attendants,
please prepare for landing.</i>

1354
01:42:46,500 --> 01:42:48,333
Talk all you want while you can.

1355
01:42:48,417 --> 01:42:51,208
You're about to die
with everyone else on this plane.

1356
01:42:51,292 --> 01:42:53,292
I don't even have to shoot you again.

1357
01:42:53,375 --> 01:42:54,875
All I have to do…

1358
01:42:58,958 --> 01:43:00,167
is nothing.

1359
01:43:12,292 --> 01:43:13,750
You think bombs spoil?

1360
01:43:14,667 --> 01:43:15,708
Nice work.

1361
01:43:18,292 --> 01:43:20,542
Still wanna know
why I flunked that polygraph?

1362
01:43:20,625 --> 01:43:25,750
No, thanks. I'm gonna be busy
setting up my parachute and my bomb.

1363
01:43:27,208 --> 01:43:30,208
They asked if I ever saw a crime
that you didn't report.

1364
01:43:30,292 --> 01:43:32,000
Let me guess. Your dad, right?

1365
01:43:32,083 --> 01:43:33,083
Yeah.

1366
01:43:33,167 --> 01:43:36,875
Lifted a few bucks from the till?
You lied for sad old Dad, huh?

1367
01:43:36,958 --> 01:43:39,083
I was just trying to protect him.

1368
01:43:39,167 --> 01:43:41,042
I never was much of a liar.

1369
01:43:41,125 --> 01:43:44,000
Yeah? Well, you protected him
and then they threw you out

1370
01:43:44,083 --> 01:43:46,375
and you've been like him
ever since, right?

1371
01:43:47,375 --> 01:43:50,792
A loser, a waste, and asleep.

1372
01:43:58,833 --> 01:44:00,375
I guess I woke up.

1373
01:44:09,000 --> 01:44:10,292
Ethan!

1374
01:45:28,875 --> 01:45:30,208
Freeze!

1375
01:45:32,083 --> 01:45:33,208
Stay right there.

1376
01:45:33,292 --> 01:45:35,875
On your knees! On your knees!

1377
01:45:35,958 --> 01:45:39,500
No, wait! Don't shoot! I'm not the guy!
I'm not the… guy!

1378
01:45:39,583 --> 01:45:41,083
FD set up in five.

1379
01:45:41,167 --> 01:45:42,042
Plain sight.

1380
01:45:42,125 --> 01:45:43,125
Let's go!

1381
01:45:44,583 --> 01:45:46,792
- Set up a perimeter.
- Let him go.

1382
01:45:46,875 --> 01:45:49,708
- Set up triage over there!
<i>- Intercept in 30 seconds.</i>

1383
01:45:52,000 --> 01:45:53,208
Where's the Novichok?

1384
01:45:53,292 --> 01:45:55,083
Vacuum-sealed in a fridge.

1385
01:45:55,167 --> 01:45:56,458
And the guy?

1386
01:45:56,542 --> 01:45:57,542
Same fridge.

1387
01:45:59,417 --> 01:46:01,167
We've got a dispersed nerve agent.

1388
01:46:01,250 --> 01:46:04,125
Send in Hazmat,
get all these passengers out of here now.

1389
01:46:04,208 --> 01:46:06,333
- Yes, ma'am.
- Get him to a medic.

1390
01:46:11,417 --> 01:46:12,625
- No, ma'am.
- Ethan!

1391
01:46:12,708 --> 01:46:15,000
- No, we can't have you go in right now.
- Hey.

1392
01:46:15,083 --> 01:46:17,417
- Nobody's going any further.
- Let her through.

1393
01:46:22,667 --> 01:46:24,208
- Are you okay?
- Are you okay?

1394
01:46:24,292 --> 01:46:25,625
- Yeah.
- Yeah.

1395
01:46:25,708 --> 01:46:27,625
Set up a perimeter over there.

1396
01:46:28,708 --> 01:46:30,333
I knew you could do it.

1397
01:46:32,208 --> 01:46:33,625
Hazmat.

1398
01:46:36,000 --> 01:46:37,958
Watch your steps coming down, folks.

1399
01:46:43,250 --> 01:46:44,583
I love you.

1400
01:46:45,250 --> 01:46:46,458
I love you.

1401
01:46:57,833 --> 01:46:59,250
Yeah, I'm sorry I hit you.

1402
01:46:59,333 --> 01:47:01,917
Mmm-hmm. You got good instincts, Kopek.

1403
01:47:03,833 --> 01:47:05,875
Call me when you get that stitched up.

1404
01:47:42,250 --> 01:47:44,417
Yeah.

1405
01:47:54,542 --> 01:47:56,208
- Hey.
- Hey.

1406
01:47:56,292 --> 01:47:57,708
Tahiti today?

1407
01:47:57,792 --> 01:47:59,000
About time.

1408
01:47:59,833 --> 01:48:02,667
Ooh, so cute. But maybe we can do this
on the other side.

1409
01:48:02,750 --> 01:48:05,167
- Yes, sir.
- This line is ridiculous.

1410
01:48:05,250 --> 01:48:07,833
How long does it take you
to wave a wand over an old lady?

1411
01:48:07,917 --> 01:48:09,042
Hey!

1412
01:48:09,625 --> 01:48:11,208
She's just doing her job.

1413
01:48:13,125 --> 01:48:14,208
Happy Christmas.

1414
01:48:18,917 --> 01:48:20,375
All right. Let's go.

1415
01:48:20,833 --> 01:48:23,667
Yo, left foot, right foot,
left foot, right foot…

1416
01:48:24,667 --> 01:48:25,792
Oh…